<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:0d4cdce4b8dbfc78504bcc4da74aaffecf567385>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The Australian Marine Microbial Biodiversity Initiative (AMMBI) provides methodologically standardized, continental scale, temporal phylogenetic amplicon sequencing data describing Bacteria, Archaea and microbial Eukarya assemblages. Sequence data is linked to extensive physical, biological and chemical oceanographic contextual information. Samples are collected monthly to seasonally from multiple depths at seven National Reference Stations (NRS) sites: Darwin Harbour (Northern Territory), Yongala (Queensland), North Stradbroke Island (Queensland), Port Hacking (New South Wales), Maria Island (Tasmania), Kangaroo Island (South Australia), Rottnest Island (Western Australia). The Integrated Marine Observing System (IMOS) NRS network is described at http://imos.org.au/facilities/nationalmooringnetwork/nrs/
North Stradbroke Island NRS is located 6.6 nm north east of North Stradbroke Island at a depth of 60 m over sandy substrate. It is 30 km southeast of the major city of Brisbane, Queensland (population 2.099 million), at the opening to large, shallow, Moreton Bay. The site is impacted by the southerly flowing EAC and its eddies, which may cause periodic nutrient enrichment through upwelling. This latitude is the biogeographic boundary for many tropical and subtropical species. The water column is well mixed between May-August and stratified for the remainder of the year and salinity may at times be affected by floodwaters from the nearby Brisbane River outflow.


 
 Site details from Brown, M. V. et al. Continental scale monitoring of marine microbiota by the Australian Marine Microbial Biodiversity Initiative. Sci. Data 5:180130 doi: 10.1038/sdata.2018.130 (2018).
Site location: North Stradbroke Island  National Reference Station (NRS), Queensland, Australia
Note on data download/processing:
Data downloaded from Australian Microbiome Initiative via Bioplatforms Australia Data Portal on 17 June 2022. The search filter applied to download data from Bioplatforms Australia Data portal are stored in the Darwin Core property (identificationRemarks). Taxonomy is assigned according to the taxonomic database (SILVA 138) and method (Sklearn) which is stored in the Darwin Core Extension
DNA derived data property (otu_db). Prefix were removed from the taxonomic names as shown in the example (e.g. d__Bacteria to Bacteria). Scientific name is assigned to the valid name available from the highest taxonomic rank.
This collection is published as Darwin Core Occurrence, so the event level measurements need to be replicated for every occurrence. Instead of data replication, the event level eMoF data are made available separately at https://www.marine.csiro.au/data/services/obisau/emof_export.cfm?ipt_resource=bioplatforms_mm_nrs_nsi
Please see https://www.australianmicrobiome.com/protocols/acknowledgements/ for citation examples and links to the data policy.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "occurrence, 16S rRNA, 18S rRNA" ;
    ecsummary:name "Marine Microbes from the North Stradbroke Island  National Reference Station (NRS), Queensland, Australia (2012-2020)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/74d67d71-2d25-4fa1-9a1e-df71c6af891e> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:0d631e3464321f4dfe20dc9acbc97b08e3ac72be>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
HDR Environmental, Operations and Construction, Inc.

Dataset credits:
The U.S. Navy Marine Species Monitoring Program

Abstract:
Features in this feature class represent animal sightings that occurred during four aerial surveys for marine mammals performed in July 2014, September 2014, January 2015 and April 2015 in the Puget Sound, WA. Surveys followed line-transect protocol and were designed to collect data for estimation of abundance and density of marine mammals. Survey dates were 21 to 27 July 2014, 14 to 21 September 2014, 5 to 12 January 2015 and 15 to 22 April 2015. Work was performed under HDR task order JP04 (IDIQ contract award N62470-10-D-3011, NAVFAC LANT).

Supplemental information:
A full version of downloadable data (ESRI personal geodatabase) including all attributes submitted is available upon request.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Northwest Training Range Complex,Marine Animal Survey,Marine Biology,Marine mammals,Visual Sighting,Aircraft, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "NWTRC JP04 Aerial Surveys 2014-2015" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/2c88fa97-db06-4669-b0dc-9690eba73a93> ;
.

