<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:15844f351841061f74f16252817ab966261cdf37>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """El presente conjunto de datos contiene a los nematodos de las Colecciones Biológicas adscritas al Centro de Colecciones Científicas (CCC) de la Universidad del Magdalena. El recurso cuenta actualmente con 203 registros biológicos de especímenes que fueron recolectados en distintos puntos del Caribe colombiano, tanto en áreas costeras como profundas. La totalidad del material disponible hasta el momento, fue obtenido de proyectos desarrollados por entidades externas que lo han depositado en la colección. Los especímenes están depositados bajo el acrónimo CBUMAG: NMA.
La colección fue documentada, digitalizada y publicada por primera vez durante la ejecución del proyecto BID-CA2020-055-NAC "Incremento de la accesibilidad de información marina de las Colecciones de Historia Natural de Colombia, mediante la movilización de datos, el fortalecimiento de la infraestructura y el entrenamiento". El presente conjunto de datos es el producto de dicho proceso realizado entre 2021-07-01 y 2023-06-30, como parte del entregable “Colección de biología marina del Centro de Colecciones Biológicas de la Universidad del Magdalena – CBUMAG” aportado por la UniMagdalena al proyecto.
This data set contains the nematodes from the Biological Collections attached to the Center for Scientific Collections (CCC) of the Universidad del Magdalena. The resource currently has 203 biological records of specimens that were collected in different parts of the Colombian Caribbean, both in coastal and deep areas. All the material available to date was obtained from projects developed by external entities that have deposited it in the collection. The specimens are deposited under the acronym CBUMAG: NMA.
The collection was documented, digitized and published for the first time during the execution of the BID-CA2020-055-NAC project "Increasing the accessibility of marine information of the Natural History Collections of Colombia, through data mobilization, infrastructure strengthening and training". The present dataset is the product of that process carried out between 2021-07-01 and 2023-06-30, as part of the deliverable "Marine Biology Collection of the Biological Collections Center of the University of Magdalena - CBUMAG" contributed by UniMagdalena to the project.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Nematoda, Nematodos, Caribe colombiano, Marino, Colección biológica, Universidad del Magdalena, CBUMAG, Specimen" ;
    ecsummary:name "Nematodos de las Colecciones Biológicas de la Universidad del Magdalena" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/56ec9691-75c7-4d30-bd66-773e05ca98d8> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:1592ea8e88ded9a772f42c9665b4e5acb6193cff>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This data consists of counts of putative zooplankton OTUs, revealed through metabarcoding of the cytochrome oxidase I (COI) gene extracted from filtered water samples in the Florida Keys National Marine Sanctuary during 2016. It includes results from 95 water samples taken over three days at three coral reef sites. After data processing, a total of 194 taxa were identified; the identification was to the species level, with only a few to the genus level. " ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, zooplankton, DNA sequencing, molecular taxonomy, biodiversity, ocean environment, Observation, COI" ;
    ecsummary:name "Marine zooplankton community structure through environmental DNA metabarcoding in the Florida Keys, collected by the South Florida Program (NOAA/AOML) and the Marine Biodiversity Observation Network (MBON)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/b41e10e2-5717-4bb3-b06a-7840a62aebcc> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:15ac89eb3a97083c259dee8a39277198d36a1262>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """This study investigates the faunal biodiversity of the deep water sediments of Grand Manan Basin in the Bay Fundy on the East Coast of North America. Specimens were collected using a 0.1 m2 grab, and identified and enumerated at the Atlantic Reference Centre. The sediment types at the research sites were found to be complex containing cobbles, pebbles, sand and clay. The specimens retrieved from these samples showed a great degree of biodiversity, and include species not previously reported in this region.

Version 1 of this resource was created as a Census of Marine Life dataset in 2005.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "oceans, biota, biological classification, Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Grand Manan Basin Benthos" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/29a7f240-6dca-4da8-87fd-3d1173fbfb1b> ;
.

