<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:184c199382feed4dc6888c3e19f3765626be9958>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """El phylum Nemertea está formado por un pequeño grupo de invertebrados con alrededor de 1400 especies, principalmente marinas de vida libre, asociados al bentos, solo un pequeño grupo de especies son parásitas. La principal característica de este phylum es la presencia de una trompa o probóscide retráctil, alojada dentro de una cavidad hidrostática independiente del sistema digestivo llamada rincocele, probóscide útil para la captura de sus presas, entre las que se destacan crustáceos, moluscos y poliquetos.
El presente conjunto de datos contiene a los nemertinos de las Colecciones Biológicas adscritas al Centro de Colecciones Científicas (CCC) de la Universidad del Magdalena. Este recurso cuenta actualmente con 221 registros biológicos de especímenes que fueron recolectados en distintas localidades del Caribe colombiano en áreas costeras, principalmente en el litoral rocoso de la ciudad de Santa Marta (Magdalena), entre los 0 y 14 m de profundidad. El 100% de los lotes fueron depositados en la colección por personal de la Universidad, como producto de actividades académicas y de investigación. Los especímenes están depositados bajo el acrónimo CBUMAG: NEM.
Las especies depositadas en esta colección han permitido abrir nuevas perspectivas de investigación en diferentes líneas de las ciencias marinas en Colombia que van desde la taxonomía, biología pesquera, y bioprospección. Se hace necesario seguir investigando los nemertinos de Colombia ya que a pesar de que se han realizado algunas investigaciones estas se concentran en un área geográfica limitada.
122 registros incluidos en esta versión fueron documentados y publicados en el marco del proyecto "Incremento de la accesibilidad de información marina de las Colecciones de Historia Natural de Colombia, mediante la movilización de datos, el fortalecimiento de la infraestructura y el entrenamiento" implementado entre 2021-07-01 y 2023-06-30 bajo la coordinación del Instituto de Investigación Marinas y Costeras - INVEMAR, y en convenio con la Red Nacional de Museos de Ciencia, Historia Natural y Colecciones Biológicas, SiB Colombia, SiBM-OBIS, GBIF y otras cinco colecciones nacionales. Durante esta iniciativa se buscó el fortalecimiento de las colecciones biológicas del país, enfocándose en especímenes marinos para facilitar su acceso a través de la movilización de datos hacia los sistemas de información de biodiversidad nacionales y globales.
The phylum Nemertea is made up of a small group of invertebrates with around 1400 species, mainly free-living marine, associated with the benthos, only a small group of species are parasites. The main characteristic of this phylum is the presence of a retractable proboscis or proboscis, housed within a hydrostatic cavity independent of the digestive system called rhynchocele, a proboscis useful for capturing its prey, among which crustaceans, mollusks, and polychaetes stand out.
This data set contains the Nemerteans from the Biological Collections attached to the Center for Scientific Collections (CCC) of the Universidad del Magdalena. This resource currently has 221 biological records of specimens that were collected in different localities of the Colombian Caribbean in coastal areas, mainly on the rocky coast of the city of Santa Marta (Magdalena), between 0 and 14 m deep. 100% of the lots were deposited in the collection by University personnel, as a product of academic and research activities. The specimens are deposited under the acronym CBUMAG: NEM.
The species deposited in this collection have opened up new research perspectives in different lines of marine science in Colombia, ranging from taxonomy, fisheries biology, and bioprospecting. It is necessary to continue investigating the Nemerteans of Colombia since, despite the fact that some investigations have been carried out, they are concentrated in a limited geographical area.
122 records included in this version were documented and published within the framework of the project "Increase the accessibility of marine information from the Natural History Collections of Colombia, through data mobilization, strengthening of infrastructure and training" implemented between 2021-07-01 and 2023-06-30 under the coordination of the Marine and Coastal Research Institute - INVEMAR; the National Network of Science Museums, Natural History, and Biological Collections; SiB Colombia; SiBM-OBIS; GBIF, and five other national collections. During this initiative, the aim was to strengthen the country's biological collections, focusing on marine specimens to facilitate their access through the mobilization of data to national and global biodiversity information systems.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Specimen, Nemertea, Nemertinos, Caribe colombiano, Marino, Colección biológica, Universidad del Magdalena, CBUMAG, PERMISO_COLECTA, SIB_MARINO, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "Nemertinos de las Colecciones Biológicas de la Universidad del Magdalena" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/0abb8cc1-8651-4213-aff3-2153d14ac322> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:184d0989967bd15350a5f94836a9c1d2f394050e>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "<p>This dataset provides access to cetacean sighting records collected throughout the historical series of PELACUS surveys, from 2007 to 2022.</p><p>The PELACUS survey is an annual survey for the evaluation of fishing resources organized by the Spanish Institute of Oceanography (IEO-CSIC) that has incorporated top predators’ (marine mammals, birds and turtles) observers since 2007. The spatial coverage of this survey covers the continental shelf waters in the north and northwest of the Iberian Peninsula, comprising Spanish waters found between the coast and the 1000 meters isobath, from the northern border with Portugal, at the mouth of the Miño River, to the border with France in the Bay of Biscay. This survey has carried out additional transects in some of its editions, sampling on the continental shelf of northern Portugal, as well as the French slope in the Bay of Biscay. Data on sightings in these areas are included.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Cetacea, Spain, Continental shelf, Samplingevent" ;
    ecsummary:name "Cetacean sightings of PELACUS surveys: Continental shelf of Galicia and Bay of Biscay - Database of the Spanish Institute of Oceanography (IEO-CSIC)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/a9818622-ac1a-4690-a26f-7e57f387bf5c> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:184f84babe6ddf23d81057c9ab0ea15a1f78be55>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
HDR Environmental, Operations and Construction, Inc.

Dataset credits:
The U.S. Navy Marine Species Monitoring Program

Abstract:
Aerial surveys for marine-species monitoring occurred during 22 through 28 June 2013 for a Small Synthetic Aperture Minehunter 2 (SSAM2) and Buried Object Scanning Sonar (BOSS) test event. These surveys were conducted off the west coast of Florida in the Naval Surface Warfare Center Panama City Division (NSWC PCD) Study Area in the Gulf of Mexico. The SSAM2 is a bottom-mapping and mine-hunting sonar developed for use in shallow-water and nearshore environments. The BOSS is a sonar system that images buried objects.

Purpose:
U.S. Navy protected marine species survey during SSAM2 and BOSS testing""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Navy project,Aircraft,Sightings, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "Sightings for SSAM2-BOSS Sonar Test Event - June 2013" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/4db4467c-f66d-4a92-acfd-b3b9974fc0af> ;
.

