<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:1997129a9fc2067ad9f23f28c3e88e025d67fb89>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
North Carolina Aquariums

Dataset credits:
Data provider
NC Aquariums Cold Stunned Sea Turtle Monitoring
Originating data center
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/">Satellite Tracking and Analysis Tool (STAT)</a>
Project sponsor or sponsor description
This project is supported by the Triad Foundation


Abstract:
Every year, cold-stunned sea turtles strand on North Carolina beaches.  Rehabilitation centers, including the North Carolina Aquariums, assist the rescue effort by providing care and returning these animals to good health.  These turtles are then released offshore into the warm waters of the Gulf Stream, and this project aims to understand where young green turtles go and how they fare in this environment after recovering from cold stunning.

Supplemental information:
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/index.shtml?project_id=705">Visit STAT's project page</a> for additional information.

This dataset is a summarized representation of the telemetry locations aggregated per species per 1-degree cell.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "NC Aquariums Cold Stunned Sea Turtle Monitoring (aggregated per 1-degree cell)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/1bc1fe8f-4485-4342-92a0-b87d61b7e826> ;
.

