<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:1bd3c02118f7823659dc9c98870162cff21f6dc2>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The movements, diving behaviour and thermal environment occupied by female olive ridley turtles Lepidochelys olivacea in northern Australia were determined through satellite telemetry, during the post-nesting migration. Satellite-relayed data loggers (SRDLs) were attached to the carapaces of 4 female olive ridley turtles nesting in the Wessel Islands of Arnhem Land in the Northern Territory of Australia (Graham Island: 11° 45’ S, 135° 57’ E and Wunpirri Island: 11° 36’ S, 136° 05’ E)
Data downloaded from IMOS 14-June-2017 from https://portal.aodn.org.au/search?uuid=6bed374a-3e86-4bbb-b8d1-a6bf8e2fa183 and taxonomy matched to WoRMS.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Satellite tracking of female olive ridley sea turtles (Lepidochelys olivacea) nesting in the Wessel Islands, Northern Territory, 2005" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/fe40f69a-3539-48b8-9836-4ccb91a89e56> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:1bd67156f934343aeeead85535e53ba2d4fdaa49>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
HDR Environmental, Operations and Construction, Inc.

Dataset credits:
The U.S. Navy Marine Species Monitoring Program

Abstract:
The marine mammal and sea turtle monitoring, vessel- and aerial-based surveys, were conducted
between November 11–23, 2010, before, during, and after the Pacific Fleet training event in the
HRC.
The objectives of the vessel-based monitoring effort for Koa Kai 11-1 consisted of the following:

- Perform focal behavioral follows of marine mammals during the course of a training event
involving ASW
- Assess the occurrence, distribution, and behavior of target species (marine mammals and
sea turtles) using a vessel-based line transect survey within the HRC in waters within or
adjacent to the area where ships were training
- Locate individual false killer whales (Pseudorca crassidens), pygmy killer whales (Feresa
attenuata), and short-finned pilot whales (Globicephala macrorhynchus) tagged by
Dr. Robin Baird with Cascadia Research
- Investigate the occurrence, distribution, and behavior of target species (marine mammals
and sea turtles) using vessel-based line transect survey in waters within or adjacent to the
area where Navy ships were training.

Purpose:
not provided

Supplemental information:
[2017-10-13] Data fields are changed so that they follow other Navy datasets.

[2014-11-19] The dataset name was changed, replacing 2011 with 2010.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Hawaii Range Complex,Vessel,Sightings, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "HRC Koa Kai-11 Marine Species Monitoring Vessel Surveys November 2010" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/2c699271-3a7f-4197-bbe8-84690c53264b> ;
.

