<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:1d3f54d5d63be7cf65c5510a2a340945248f3523>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "These data are amplicon sequence variant (ASV) counts of marine fish derived from environmental DNA (eDNA) sampling targeting the 12S rDNA, V5 region. DNA was extracted from filtered water samples taken off coastal New Jersey during the 2019 New Jersey Ocean Trawl Survey. Sampling corresponded to the New Jersey Ocean Trawl Survey efforts, but trawl data are not included here. The data were originally published as supplementary tables in support of Stoeckle et al. (https://doi.org/10.1093/icesjms/fsaa225). Observations from supplementary tables 8A - 8D were subsequently aligned to Darwin Core." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "FISH (UUID: ea855d4c-f132-44f9-b31c-447e1101684d), TRAWL (UUID: c386fdd8-5a49-46c6-9be6-b56a9428f30d), NERITIC ZONE (UUID: eb958dfb-5e38-401f-8b42-5f1273c75a4a), ATLANTIC OCEAN (UUID: cf249a36-2e82-4d32-84cd-23a4f40bb393), NEW JERSEY (UUID: 699b0e5a-6dbd-47aa-b0ca-c4502f044e35), marine biome (ENVO:00000447), coastal water (ENVO:00001250), waterborne particulate matter (ENVO:01000436), marine biota (ENVO: 06105013), Environmental DNA (NCIT:C169196), Fish (NCIT:C14207), Occurrence, 12S rDNA" ;
    ecsummary:name "eDNA observations, concurrent with trawl survey, of marine fish in coastal New Jersey, USA 2019" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/fe2ed263-2b21-47d7-a79f-f9b911132398> ;
