.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:24d69444ca839e3f00e3954a24679063a8a7478d>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """In 2019 (late August to early September), the Natural History Museum of Los Angeles County led a two-week expedition to the urban ocean waters of the Los Angeles region to improve our knowledge of Southern California marine biodiversity. This program brought together the best taxonomists and local collectors in an internationally recognized, intensive methodology to collect, live-identify, curate, and DNA barcode as many species as possible.

The pop-up marine science lab at AltaSea processed fresh samples from research ships and live specimens from SCUBA divers. A team of leading taxonomists assembled for the event sorted, identified, and sampled specimens for genetic analysis, all day, every day.
This also was a wonderful opportunity for the public to take a peek into a major marine research program being carried out at the coast of a major urban center.

The Los Angeles Urban Ocean Expedition was a program of the Marine Biodiversity Center at the Natural History Museum.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Specimen" ;
    ecsummary:name "Los Angeles Urban Ocean Expedition 2019" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/92af50ad-c9d7-4fe7-b012-eae0e77233a2> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:24e15b13e969d03f6f03dfe2fbd15bbc3d615665>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The Arctic Laboratories were commissioned to undertake a combined chemical, biological and physical oceanographic survey from March 1981 to April 1982 in the vicinity of the Issungnak O-61 artificial island. Because of its position near the 20m depth contour, the island provided an ideal opportunity to study oceanographic features in a transitional zone between the more truly marine waters of the outer shelf and Mackenzie River dominated water of shallower nearshore regions.  

This resource contains species presence information collected during benthic macroinvertebrate surveys conducted concurrently with the oceanographic parameters at the same three stations around Issungnak from June 1981 to April 1982.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "MacroBenthos collected at Issungnak Artificial Island in Southern Beaufort Sea, 1981-1982" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/4b3c7211-bb96-4373-9ddf-73424e92c882> ;
.

