<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:2648311298332559c376e2a157368ee884a270a2>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """El presente conjunto de datos contiene a los tunicados de las Colecciones Biológicas adscritas al Centro de Colecciones Científicas (CCC) de la Universidad del Magdalena. Este recurso cuenta con 3 registros de tunicados pertenecientes a la Clase Ascidiacea, todos provenientes de diferentes sitios del Caribe colombiano esto incluye la zona costera y también de mar abierto. Los especímenes están depositados bajo el acrónimo CBUMAG: TUN.
La colección fue documentada, digitalizada y publicada por primera vez durante la ejecución del proyecto BID-CA2020-055-NAC "Incremento de la accesibilidad de información marina de las Colecciones de Historia Natural de Colombia, mediante la movilización de datos, el fortalecimiento de la infraestructura y el entrenamiento". El presente conjunto de datos es el producto de dicho proceso realizado entre 2021-07-01 y 2023-06-30, como parte del entregable “Colección de biología marina del Centro de Colecciones Biológicas de la Universidad del Magdalena – CBUMAG” aportado por la UniMagdalena al proyecto.
This data set contains the tunicates from the Biological Collections attached to the Center for Scientific Collections (CCC) of the Universidad del Magdalena. This resource has 3 records of tunicates belonging to the Ascidiacea Class, all from different sites in the Colombian Caribbean, this includes the coastal zone and also the open sea. The specimens are deposited under the acronym CBUMAG: TUN.
The collection was documented, digitized and published for the first time during the execution of the BID-CA2020-055-NAC project "Increasing the accessibility of marine information of the Natural History Collections of Colombia, through data mobilization, infrastructure strengthening and training". The present dataset is the product of that process carried out between 2021-07-01 and 2023-06-30, as part of the deliverable "Marine Biology Collection of the Biological Collections Center of the University of Magdalena - CBUMAG" contributed by UniMagdalena to the project.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Specimen, CBUMAG, Chordata, Caribe colombiano, marino" ;
    ecsummary:name "Tunicados de las Colecciones Biológicas de la Universidad del Magdalena" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/610d407f-2378-4a70-a203-27f6901d43cb> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:264e8149c3a512fc649602f4b086b476a39c0e43>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The Netherlands Indian Ocean Programme (NIOP) studied the effect of the monsoon on the climate system in the northern Indian Ocean. Information on the research themes, scientists involved and instruments used together with most of the basic scientific data gathered from May 1992 until February 1993 is available on a CDRom. It was developed in cooperation with the Netherlands Geosci. Foundation (GOA) and ETI Biodiversity Centre in the Netherlands.

Through PANGAEA, data on the abundance of dinoflagellate cysts have been made available.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Monsoons, Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "PANGAEA - data from Netherlands Indian Ocean Programme (NIOP)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/9243edbf-0c0e-4b95-a181-973223b0c78c> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:2656071b8d115c742e94a25cc31a8364922d0866>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
Happywhale

Dataset credits:
Happywhale and contributors

Abstract:
Happywhale.com is a resource to help you know whales as individuals, and to benefit conservation science with rich data about individual whales.

Supplemental information:
Sightings and images were submitted to Happywhale by contributors. A portion of the Happywhale data were transferred to OBIS-SEAMAP upon the agreement between Happywhale and OBIS-SEAMAP.

There may be duplicate records among Happywhale datasets and other OBIS-SEAMAP datasets. The precision of date/time vary per record. Some records have date accuracy up to year only.

This dataset includes sightings and photos from the following 14 contributors in alphabetic order:

Barbora Fecková; Christina Frech; Corinne Eichler; Cottele Benny; Cyril VATHELET; Espaço Talassa; Isaure Michaud; Kirsten Young; Marilia Olio; Martina Bartolini; Regina Kirkwood; Sabine+Ulf; TijsHans; Veronika Doppelreiter""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,PhotoID;Visual sighting, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "Happywhale - Risso's dolphin in North Atlantic Ocean" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/4d51c94e-8c7e-4a75-bda7-ec38912cd52d> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:2665311e32c3d09868dd171390488a54e794bf17>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
Sea Mammal Research Unit, University of St. Andrews

Dataset credits:
Sea Mammal Research Unit, University of St. Andrews

Abstract:
The Cetacean Offshore Distribution and Abundance in the European Atlantic (CODA) project estimated the abundance and investigated the habitat use of cetacean species in waters beyond the continental shelf and developed a management framework for determining safe bycatch limits for the common dolphin in this area. The results were intended primarily to inform assessments of the conservation status of all cetacean species and to help assess the impact of bycatch of common dolphin.

Supplemental information:
Surveys from seven different vessels were merged. Each vessel contained two sightings platforms running concurrently – primary and tracker. This dataset includes sightings from the primary platform. Sightings from the tracker platform are registered in <a href="/dataset/1182">CODA cetacean sightings on tracker platform of vessel surveys 2007</a>.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Marine Animal Survey,Marine Biology,Marine mammals,Visual Sighting,Vessel, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "CODA cetacean sightings on primary platform of vessel surveys 2007" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/9c893879-88a2-4bf9-9373-ecb6c594cf45> ;
.

