<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:2aed97b8d8bad6d43b7292fdd285aa1fb32049a3>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The data is the quantitative abundance of fish derived from underwater visual census methods involving transect counts at rocky reef sites around Tasmania. This data forms part of a larger dataset that also surveyed megafaunal invertebrate abundance and algal cover for the area. The aggregated dataset allows examination of changes in Tasmanian shallow reef floral and faunal communities over a decadal scale - initial surveys were conducted in 1992-1995, and again at the same sites in 2006-2007. There are plans for ongoing surveys
The originating metadata record http://metadata.imas.utas.edu.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/metadata.show?uuid=caf7220a-19e0-4a7f-9af6-eade6c79a47a contains project details, additional contacts and on-line resources.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Condition of rocky reef communities around Tasmania: fish surveys, Australia (1992-1995 and 2006-2007)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/566386e9-9494-40a1-a3a0-63233c208fee> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:2af4030cd3aab288c823082fa6c96727b57b987e>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Tracking of three fluttering shearwaters  (Puffinus gavia) from Mokohinau Islands, Hauraki Gulf in 2011-12 using geolocaters. Sea temperatures data used to correct light derived latitude estimates in some tags. Data from Zoatrack project 109 (https://zoatrack.org/projects/109/) accessed on 2021-06-08" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Tracking of fluttering shearwaters (Puffinus gavia) from Mokohinau Islands, Hauraki Gulf, New Zealand (2011-12) using geolocaters" ;
