.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:2d6424ba6cc64553dbb63be63f914b978d9a726a>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "NorFish is a European Research Council (ERC) Advanced Grant led by Prof Poul Holm in Trinity College Dublin, focuses on the premise that a 16th century shift in marine fish pricing and supply in conjunction with the Little Ice Age and lowering of sea temperatures not only rise to the North Atlantic Fish Revolution but also forms one of the first documented examples of the disrupting effects of globalisation and climate change. The project examines the role of the Fish Revolution for a range of inter-related aspects of North Atlantic history, with NorFish’s interdisciplinary team drawing on archaeology, history, cartography, geography, and ecology to develop interpretative frameworks that synthesise a broad spectrum of source data to assess the overall objective of the project. NorFish’s interdisciplinary team draws on archaeology, history, cartography, geography, and ecology to assess the objectives of the project." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Archaeology, Catch/effort, Clupeoid fisheries, Domestic consumption, History, Exports, Herrings, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "Norfish: Scottish Herring Fishery 1466-1790" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/98a42fe7-b1a2-4e1c-9ebd-782bbcb4f739> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:2d6634b19665a0d46684f7930523f7d597caa86a>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This is a historical dataset that was published in 1935 by Dr Karl Viets and concerns of some marine mites collected from Egyptian littoral waters near Alexandria. They collected during the floristical and faunistical survey of Adolf Steuer on the coasts near Alexandria mainly with the vessel “El Hoot”. This dataset covers the time span of 9/9/1933 to 13/11/1933." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Metadata" ;
    ecsummary:name "Dr.Karl Viets. 1935. The fishery grounds near Alexandria. IV. -Some Marine Mites From Alexandria. Notes and Memoirs No 11. Fisheries Research Directorate, Egypt." ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/981b3f1c-5109-4d2c-8a4b-cf1cfc535f97> ;
.

