<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:2feb705b64e6bc4c2ab96a80f7fa1302283023f8>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """This dataset was acquired on the RV Investigator voyage IN2014_E03. This was a gear trials voyage testing gear and work procedures prior to beginning scientific surveys. Full details of data, reports and publications of the voyage is at http://www.marine.csiro.au/data/trawler/survey_details.cfm?survey=IN2014_E03
Note on data download/processing:
Data downloaded from Australian Microbiome Initiative via Bioplatforms Australia Data Portal on 17 June 2022. The search filter applied to download data from Bioplatforms Australia Data portal are stored in the Darwin Core property (identificationRemarks). Taxonomy is assigned according to the taxonomic database (SILVA 138) and method (Sklearn) which is stored in the Darwin Core Extension
DNA derived data property (otu_db). Prefix were removed from the taxonomic names as shown in the example (e.g. d__Bacteria to Bacteria). Scientific name is assigned to the valid name available from the highest taxonomic rank.
This collection is published as Darwin Core Occurrence, so the event level measurements need to be replicated for every occurrence. Instead of data replication, the event level eMoF data are made available separately at https://www.marine.csiro.au/data/services/obisau/emof_export.cfm?ipt_resource=bioplatforms_mm_in2014_e03""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "occurrence, 16S rRNA, 18S rRNA" ;
    ecsummary:name "Marine Microbes from RV Investigator voyage IN2014_E03, Australia (2014)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/c82dd852-a454-4a5b-8515-ece289f382d3> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:30075c11bd6589237a27486c658e74fba2889351>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Records are presented of sightings of 6 cetacean species (15 common dolphins, Delphinus delphis Linnaeus, over 5000 dusky dolphins, Lagenorhynchus obscurus (Gray), approximately 74 bottlenose dolphins, Tursiops truncatus (Montagu), 8 sperm whales, Physeter macrocephalus Linnaeus, 6 southern humpback whales, Megaptera novaeangliae (Borowski), and 36 southern pilot whales. Globicephala melaena edwardii (Smith)) from m.v. Lloret Lopez II between 8 January and 2 April 1970. A large school of dusky dolphins was observed south of Solander Island. Monthly water temperatures in the summer of 1970 were high and in January ranged from 15.4°c (9.2 km west of Fiordland) and 21.6°c (55 km west of Cape Farewell), in February from 16.2°c (Fiordland) and 20.4°c (Cape Farewell), and in March from 16.0°c (Fiordland) and 20.5°c (Cape Farewell)." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Cetaceans sighted off the west coast of the South Island, New Zealand, Summer 1970" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/d0f7e8d3-b5ce-4ff6-bd33-2187bb6b8b46> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:300cf4cb459300b3111627ba3e77b4d3ae937fbe>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The primary objective of this voyage IN2017_V03 was to sample the biodiversity of lower bathyal (2500 m) and abyssal (4000 m) seafloor habitats off south-eastern Australia, and in particular deep-water ecosystems of seven Commonwealth marine reserves.
Data has been sourced from Atlas of Living Australia.

Voyage details (metadata, projects, other datasets either online or as downloads, publications and reports, events, maps etc) can be accessed at https://www.marine.csiro.au/data/trawler/survey_details.cfm?survey=IN2017_V03
If this data has been used in any products, please acknowledge with the following: We acknowledge the use of the CSIRO Marine National Facility (https://ror.org/01mae9353) in undertaking this research.
""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Specimen" ;
    ecsummary:name "Sampling the abyss: latitudinal biodiversity patterns along the base of Australia's eastern continental margin - RV Investigator voyage IN2017_V03, Australia (2017)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/07590136-0a80-4c78-b6b5-ad107fb56d03> ;
.

