Tethys Research Institute

Dataset credits:
Marina Costa &amp; Giuseppe Notarbartolo di Sciara, Tethys Research Institute
Sighting records were collected from the data owners:

Eritrea Project - Yohannes Mebrahtu

Israel Marine Mammal Research &amp; Assistance Center - IMMRAC
Mia Elasar, Daphna Feingold, Oz Goffman, Nir Hadar, Dan Kerem, Aviad Scheinin

Red Sea Dolphin Project - HEPCA



Abstract:
This dataset includes information about stranding occurred along: 1. the Egyptian coast of the Red Sea and collected by the MEGABase program within the Hurghada Environmental Protection and Conservation Association (HEPCA), http://www.hepca.org/
2. the Eritrean coast by Eritrea Project - Yohannes Mebrahtu
3. The Israeli coast of the Red Sea by IMMRAC

Purpose:
Gather cetacean stranding information occurred along the Red Sea and 

Supplemental information:
Stranding records were collected from the data owners:
Eritrea Project - Yohannes Mebrahtu
IMMRAC
Red Sea Dolphin Project - HEPCA

Temporal resolution varies per record. Time values are not available. "tprecision" column is added to indicate the resolution.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Marine Animal Survey,Marine Biology,Marine mammals,Visual Sighting,Land-based, Observation, Occurrence" ;
