<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:36724ca9488da8e0a2c6babd54f699d6a3157ec7>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Opportunistic sightings and strandings of Caperea marginata (n=196) from the vicinity of Australia and New Zealand (1884 to early 2007) were used to relate geographic and temporal patterns to oceanographic and broad-scale climatic variability. Records were not uniformly distributed along the coast and more (69%) were from Australia than New Zealand. Data from Appendix 1 and 2 of the cited paper." ;
