<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:4152170958b975960631ddc20349e5a61c614844>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The study was conducted at Kanowna Island (39°150 S, 146°300 E) in northern Bass Strait, southeastern Australia during the incubation and chick-rearing periods of breeding (October–January) over 4 consecutive years (2017–2021) in order to evaluate the at-sea movements of fairy prions during breeding.  There are 73 trips from adult breeding birds (N individuals = 14 and n trips = 15 in incubation; N individuals = 31 and n trips = 58 in chick-rearing). Each was equipped with a miniaturized GPS logger.
Geolocator data was also acquired but not presented here as the location errors are not known. Data was sourced from the linked repository (https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.c.5994501 ) in the cited paper on 2022-07-10.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Year-round at-sea movements of fairy prions (Pachyptila turtur)  from Kanowna Island, Bass Strait, south-eastern Australia (2017-2020)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/ca9998bc-b371-423c-a73e-de2e9e127b96> ;
.

