<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:48a81a80a7d5c6e0a8be008fda3c5358f708fccc>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Este proyecto fue concebido y diseñado primordialmente con el ánimo de llenar los vacios de información básica general sobre las caracteristicas fisiográficas, ecológicas y ambientales de las áreas con areecifes coralinos existentes en el Caribe colombiano. El proyecto abarca desde la caracterización geomorfológica y ecológica general de cada una de las áreas estudiadas, pasando por aspectos más específicos como las comunidades bióticas denominadas clave (macrolagas, peces, esponjas, corales, octocorales), hasta la evaluación de salud coralina y otros signos de deterioro ambiental. Las áreas geográficas estudiadas corresponden a las catalogadas como prioritarias en cuanto a necesidades de información en un Taller sobre Investigación y Manejo de Arrecifes Coralinos realizado en 1991 en Santa Marta." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Registros, Exploración, Areas arrecifales, Arrecifes, Caribe, Makuriwa, Corales, Moluscos, Cnidarios, Peces, Macroalgas, Bioecología, Ambiente, Evaluación, Colombia, Biodiversidad, Ecosistema, Colciencias, Arrecifes Coralinos., Occurrence, Specimen" ;
    ecsummary:name "Evaluación bioecológica y ambiental de las áreas arrecifales del Caribe colombiano" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/3b06674d-555f-4a67-8bd2-ca9c9f0755a6> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:48ab26f0940e0f6595c279558c5b5f913931c8d6>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This is a historical dataset that was published in 1937 by Th. Mortensen and Ad. Steuer and concerns of the faunistic report on the Echinoderma collected during the floristical and faunistical survey of Adolf Steuer on the coasts near Alexandria mainly with the vessel “El Hoot”. In this historical paper, there are no information about exact sampling temporal coverage. This dataset contains occurrence data of Echinoderma in the coasts of Alexandria, Egypt. It also contains information about individual counts, sex and lifestage. The digitization of this dataset was done by LifewatchGreece team." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Metadata" ;
    ecsummary:name "Mortensen Th. And Steuer Ad. 1937. The fishery grounds near Alexandria. XIII Echinoderma. Notes and Memoirs No 21. Hydrobiology and Fisheries Directorate, Egypt" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/c7f56175-96a0-4e82-b4ad-3acf55b2b46d> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:48b358c576fa989660923f5833122dc359e3efea>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The Southern Ocean Time Series (SOTS) observatory and the Subantarctic Mooring site (SAM) lie in the Subantarctic waters south west of Tasmania and south east New Zealand, respectively. The SOTS and SAM sites have been instrumented quasi-continuously with deep-moored sediment traps (≥1000 m deep) since the late 90’s - early 2000s with the main objective of quantifying sinking carbon particle fluxes to the deep sea and for a broad range of biogeochemical studies.
The E. huxleyi populations were captured by sediment traps at ~1000, 2000 and 3800 m depth for a year from August 2011 until July 2012 at the SOTS observatory and a sediment trap at ~1500 m depth for a year from November 2009 until November 2010 at the SAM site.
Full details are in Rigual-Hernández, A. S.,Trull, T. W.,Flores, J. A.,Nodder, S. D.,Eriksen, R.,Davies, D. M.,Hallegraeff, G. M.,Sierro, F. J.,Patil, S. M.,Cortina, A. (2020) Full annual monitoring of Subantarctic Emiliania huxleyi populations reveals highly calcified morphotypes in high-CO2 winter conditions. Scientific Reports 10 https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-59375-8""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Specimen" ;
    ecsummary:name "Emiliania huxleyi populations at the Subantarctic  SOTS and SAM moorings sites, Australia and New Zealand (2009-2012)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/8590681c-4cba-4857-bf00-3553c31fa1fa> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:48bfa46b27cc84b376d77271f08c9e0698c13903>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """This dataset is from a paper by Fenner a. Chace, Jr. (1955) on the shrimps of the Marshall Islands.
The collections on which the following notes are based were made during biological surveys of the northern Marshall Atolls of Eniwetok, Bikini, Rongelap, and Rongerik in 1946 and 1947, under the sponsorship of the U. S. Department of the Navy. Only the decapod shrimps of the families Penaeidae, Sergestidae, Pasiphaeidae, Processidae, Thalassocaridae, and the genera Automate and Athanas of the Alpheidae are included here.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Data from: Notes on shrimps from the Marshall Islands" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/0e34a98a-0620-42f4-89f0-494166acc80d> ;
.

