Abstract:
The marine mammal and sea turtle monitoring, vessel- and aerial-based surveys, were conducted
between November 11–23, 2010, before, during, and after the Pacific Fleet training event in the
HRC.
The objectives of the aerial?based monitoring effort for Koa Kai 11-1 was to:
- Assess the occurrence, distribution, and behavior of target species (marine mammals and
sea turtles) using a nearshore, aerial-based line transect survey in waters within or
adjacent to the area whereNavy ships were training.

Purpose:
not provided

Supplemental information:
[2017-10-13] Data fields are changed so that they follow other Navy datasets.

[2014-11-19] The dataset name was changed, replacing 2011 with 2010.""" ;
