<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:4cdaffc9e034ae0df2a5bf8303d357336e3be0c9>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Data on occurrence and distribution of deep-water organisms in Colombian territory are currently scarce. However, it is a research niche that is taking more and more prominence due to the potential of natural resources found in the deep. From 2015 to 2017 Anadarko Colombia Company (ACC) conducted hydrocarbon exploration in the southern Colombian Caribbean, assessing bottom biodiversity between 375 to 2500 meters deep. This exploratory expedition proved advantageous for the documentation of the fauna that inhabits deep-water ecosystems, using camera assessment techniques such as ROV surveys and towed cameras.  The data presented here correspond to the crustaceans encountered by ACC, which were identified to the lowest taxonomic level possible.
The data presented here corresponds to 204 occurrences of deep-sea Crustaceans. The taxonomic coverage of this dataset includes 2 class, 3 orders, 10 families, 7 genus and 1 species. There is a 2% classifed to the species level, 32% to family, 10% to order and 56% to genus.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation, Crustaceans, southern Colombian Caribbean, Deep-Sea Aristeidae, Deep-Sea Epialtidae, Deep-sea Galatheidae, Deep-Sea Geryonidae, Deep-Sea Gyphocrangonidae, Deep-Sea Munidopsidae, Deep-Sea Nematocarcinidae, Deep-Sea Paguridae, Deep-Sea Scalpellidae, ROV, towed camera, SiB_MARINO" ;
    ecsummary:name "Report of deep-sea Crustaceans (Aristeidae, Epialtidae, Galatheidae, Geryonidae, Gyphocrangonidae, Munidopsidae, Nematocarcinidae, Paguridae, Parapaguridae, Scalpellidae) in the southern Colombian Caribbean." ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/cf1034ec-9672-4802-8342-9a94609dce4f> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:4cea25c59cb8c22d1c3f698d7e124a35aaaf9c75>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Sampling occurred along 11 transects perpendicular to shore at target sampling depths of 20 m, 50 m, 100 m, 200 m, 350 m, 500 m, 750 m, and 1000 m in the Alaskan and western Canadian Beaufort Sea in the Arctic Ocean. Epibenthic communities were sampled in the summers of 2012, 2013 and 2014, with some locations resampled in subsequent years and others only sampled once, using a 3-m plumb-staff beam trawl with 7 mm mesh and 4 mm codend liner deployed for associated fish surveys. Taxa were field-identified onboard by the data providers and their research group members, and identifications of select vouchers preserved in formaldehyde-seawater solution were later confirmed or corrected by taxonomic experts (those are listed in the below listed publications). This work was partially conducted under BOEM Cooperative Agreement No. M12AC00011 US−Canada Transboundary Fish and Lower Trophic Communities,’ US Department of the Interior, BOEM, Alaska Outer Continental Shelf Region, Anchorage, Alaska, as
part of the BOEM Environmental Studies Program.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "US-CAN-Transboundary_BOEMproject_Beaufort Sea_Epibenthos_2012_2013_2014" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/837dff49-b281-4d12-a2b0-042095ff2945> ;
.

