<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:4d5a09155517e3fc1a8da622f6f5d7589ee8ca5d>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
University of North Carolina, Wilmington

Dataset credits:
William A. McLellan, University of North Carolina Wilmington

Abstract:
Aerial surveys were flown in parallel lines from the South Carolina/North Carolina border to the south end of Assateague Island, Virginia, United States from October 2005 to April 2006. All large whale, small cetaceans, sea turtles and large fish, and ship sightings were recorded. Surveys were conducted in Beaufort sea states of 5 or under and in clear weather conditions. Photos of all large whales exist in the VAB LAB photo data base at University of North Carolina Wilmington (UNCW). UNCW houses a data base that now extends from 1998 to 2006 for aerial surveys conducted in the mid-Atlantic and southeast Atlantic bight.

Purpose:
To conduct systematic aerial surveys for large whales, specifically targeting right whales, during the fall, winter and spring off North Carolina and Virginia, United States.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "UNCW Right Whale Aerial Survey 05-06" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/9a764a05-2258-4a7b-8bc9-c8ba04cccee6> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:4d5b92af3455436545906abc58d8c9d69b7f7022>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
Paolo Casale

Dataset credits:
Data provider
WWF Italy's Sea Turtle Network
Originating data center
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/">Satellite Tracking and Analysis Tool (STAT)</a>
Project partner
Questo è un progetto di WWF Italia, “Centro Cultura del Mare” A.P.S, Lega Navale di Manfredonia, Università di Roma La Sapienza ed è realizzato grazie alla collaborazione con molti pescatori di Manfredonia. Le attività a Manfredonia sono coordinate da Giovanni Simone (vicepresidente “Centro Cultura del Mare” A.P.S.), in collaborazione con la dott.ssa Gabriella Troiano, i pescatori di Manfredonia Ciro e Michele Conoscitore, Ciro e Domenico Tattilo e il Comandante della Capitaneria di Porto di Manfredonia C.F. (CP) Francesco  Staiano.This is a joint project by WWF Italy, “Centro Cultura del Mare” A.P.S, Lega Navale of Manfredonia, University of Rome La Sapienza and is possible thanks to the active collaboration of many fishers of Manfredonia. Project activities in Manfredonia are coordinated by Giovanni Simone (vice-president of “Centro Cultura del Mare” A.P.S.), in collaboration with Gabriella Troiano, the fishermen Ciro and Michele Conoscitore, Ciro and Domenico Tattilo, and the commander of the Coast Guard of Manfredonia, C.F. (CP) Francesco  Staiano.
Project sponsor or sponsor description
The Project is authorized by the Italian Ministry of Environment.


Abstract:
Il progetto intende investigare i movimenti delle tartarughe marine comuni Caretta caretta che frequentano il Golfo di Manfredonia, recentemente riconosciuto come una importante zona neritica di alimentazione per questa specie nel mar Adriatico. Le 5 tartarughe monitorate in questo progetto sono state catturate da reti a strascico nel Golfo di Manfredonia. Per ridurre al minimo lo stress per gli animali, le trasmittenti satellitari sono state applicate appena possibile dopo l’arrivo delle tartarughe al porto e le tartarughe sono state rilasciate subito dopo.This project aims to investigate the movement patterns of loggerhead sea turtles frequenting the Gulf of Manfredonia, which was recently recognized as an important neritic foraging ground for this species in the Adriatic Sea. The 5 turtles monitored by this project were incidentally caught by trawlers fishing in the Gulf. In order to minimize the stress induced, the satellite trasmitters were attached as soon as possible after turtle landing, then turtles were immediately released .

Supplemental information:
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/index.shtml?project_id=751">Visit STAT's project page</a> for additional information.

This dataset is a summarized representation of the telemetry locations aggregated per species per 1-degree cell.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "WWF Italy - Manfredonia (aggregated per 1-degree cell)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/982690d2-6f22-4753-a748-89528833d5da> ;
.

