<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:5aecb3fae6e6233e283347c591081c8230c087ed>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
NOAA Southwest Fisheries Science Center (SWFSC)

Dataset credits:
NOAA Southwest Fisheries Science Center (SWFSC)

Purpose:
CCES = California Current Ecosystem Survey
Objective: Joint survey for coastal pelagic fish stock, cetaceans and seabirds, to update fish and cetacean stock assessments and study spatial predator-prey relationships.  
Vessel: NOAA Ship Reuben Lasker.  
Study area: waters off the west coasts of southern Canada (Vancouver Island), U.S., and northern Mexico (Baja California).

Supplemental information:
SWFSC MMTD Cruise Number: 1651
Perpendicular distance will be released upon permission by the contributor. Please contact the contributor if needed.

Attribute descriptions for effort data:
dist: Length of the segment (km) 
Mode: Effort mode type (C = closing mode; P = passing mode)""" ;
