<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:5e98ac0602de96fb537cb6f4895d61709fdd3816>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
Marine Research Foundation

Dataset credits:
Data provider
Marine Research Foundation - Marine Turtle Programme
Originating data center
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/">Satellite Tracking and Analysis Tool (STAT)</a>
Project sponsor or sponsor description
This project is funded in part by the Mohammed bin Zayed Species Conservation Fund, the Forestry Bureau of Taiwan, and the Shell (Malaysia) Foundation.


Abstract:
Juvenile turtles recruit at Mantanani from their post-hatchling neritic drifting years at some 30 cm in CCL and reside there for some 5-6 years and they subsequently depart to secondary foraging grounds - presently unknown. This project will track small (40-60 cm CCL) green turtles as they depart Mantanani to identify the location of the secondary foraging areas. For conservation to be successful, we aim to inform governments and conservaiton agencies of the connectivity of marine habitats with this work.

Supplemental information:
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/index.shtml?project_id=593">Visit STAT's project page</a> for additional information.

This dataset is a summarized representation of the telemetry locations aggregated per species per 1-degree cell.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Marine Biology, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "Identification of secondary foraging grounds for green turtles as they depart Mantanani, Malaysia (aggregated per 1-degree cell)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/282c67f7-d6f1-4c9f-9efe-8e3a20539807> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:5e9af4f246bf53a9e831742b0d83c7f0210d4a2c>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Since September 2017, the TAMS LTER has been continuously monitoring zooplankton in the estuarine plume area of the Mamucabas and Ilhetas rivers, also covering Tamandaré Bay and the adjacent reefs. This research has generated robust data on the structure of the microzooplankton and mesozooplankton communities in the areas under study. Monitoring has been carried out by the Laboratório de Ecologia do Plâncton (LEPLANC/UFRPE), Laboratório de Zooplâncton (LabZoo/UFPE) and Laboratório de Fitoplâncton (LabFito/UFPE). The results obtained have been fundamental in elucidating the biogeochemical effects of the estuarine plume on reef ecosystems, showing changes in the trophic structure along the salinity gradient, from the estuarine plume zone to the coastal reefs. These data contribute significantly to understanding ecological interactions and the responses of zooplankton organisms to environmental variations induced by estuarine dynamics." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Samplingevent, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "PELD - TAMS | Monitoring the spatio-temporal heterogeneity of zooplankton, considering the connectivity between the estuaries, bay and coastal reefs of Tamandaré Bay" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/0ef62745-06f7-4251-9eb9-cccf8ed5dc2b> ;
.

