<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:614bb3d08e7cd3d6506c2995c2ea7e9b5e64d5fd>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "A checklist containing 29 species of reef fishes recorded at the gulfs San José and Nuevo in Argentina (~42º–43ºS) is provided. The reef-fish assemblages of the San José and Nuevo gulfs are a mix of warm-temperate fauna from the South-western Atlantic Province, and cold-temperate species from the South-American Province; however, warmtemperate fishes dominated in both gulfs. The presence of the families Bovichtidae, Eleginopidae, Nototheniidae, Congiopodidae, Sebastidae and Moridae distinguished the Patagonian region from the rest of the Atlantic coast." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "The Reef-fish Fauna of the Northern Patagonian Gulfs, Argentina, South-western Atlantic: Fishes Checklist" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/3e3119d8-b834-4ecf-bcfd-38af1c09f275> ;
.

