<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:616c9bd3684db700fe4449caaffda4dadff4ef71>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This dataset describes the abyssal megafaunal mollusc morphotypes observed during the two ABYSSLINE cruises (AB01/MV1313 - 2013 and AB02/TN319 - 2015) to the UKSRL polymetallic-nodule exploration contract area (UK-1) and the site EPIRB (~250 km east of the UK-1 area) in the Clarion-Clipperton Zone in the Pacific Ocean. These megafaunal molluscs were recorded using ROV and AUV. There appear to be at least 4 distinct morphospecies identified by imagery. This dataset is from the paper: Amon D, Ziegler A, Drazen J, Grischenko A, Leitner A, Lindsay D, Voight J, Wicksten M, Young C, Smith C (2017) Megafauna of the UKSRL exploration contract area and eastern Clarion-Clipperton Zone in the Pacific Ocean: Annelida, Arthropoda, Bryozoa, Chordata, Ctenophora, Mollusca. Biodiversity Data Journal 5: e14598. https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.5.e14598" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence; Deep-sea mining; Polymetallic nodule; Clarion-Clipperton Zone; megafauna; Mollusca" ;
    ecsummary:name "abyssline_uksrl_contract_area_ccz_megafauna_2013-2015_mollusca" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/a7a1ee38-425e-44be-af06-480e33889d03> ;
.

