<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:622c72447e2460bb6ec5f0c69bd89fdd5a50faca>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """In January 1949, as a result of continued concern over declining abundance of stocks throughout the Northwest Atlantic, the International Convention for the Northwest Atlantic Fisheries (ICNAF) was established.  The stated purpose of the Convention was the investigation, protection and conservation of the fisheries. For a history of this organization please refer to Emory D. Anderson J. yyyy

The ICNAF NORWESTLANT Surveys took place during April to July 1963.  The dates of the three surveys which were carried out were as follows:
NORWESTLANT 1: 31 March - 9 May
NORWESTLANT 2: 30 April - 30 June
NORWESTLANT 3: 30 June - 3 August

The object of the study was to give an account of the distribution of zooplankton which may be relevant to the distribution and survival of cod and redfish larvae. The dataset concerns a very wide area and is not intended as a comprehensive review of the zooplankton. In addition to plankton distribution the expedition reports also contains a short section on marine mammal observations.

This resource contains data extracts from the published report for marine mammal observations recorded by the ships officers and scientists.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "NAFO/ICNAF - Environmental Surveys - NORWESTLANT 1-3, 1963: Marine mammals observations" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/bf496057-5891-4bc4-88e1-f20c18032fe7> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:6231153e495efb1667fa20cf7d5efccd9dc773ba>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "These data represent the macroalgal composition of eight reefs from the Campeche Bank: Banco Nuevo Reef (BN), Banco Obispo Norte Reef (BON), Banco Obispo Sur Reef (BOS), Banco Pera Reef (BP), Cayo Arenas Reef, Triángulo Oeste Reef (TO), Triángulo Este Reef (TE), and Serpientes Reef (Ser). Sampling was conducted using self-contained underwater breathing apparatus (SCUBA), free diving, and general intertidal collection methods. All samples obtained were identified to the lowest possible taxonomic level and added to the Algae section of the Herbarium of the Faculty of Sciences of UNAM. Three new records for this region are documented: Ceratodictyon scoparium (Montagne &amp; Millardet) R.E.Norris, 1987, Herposiphonia parca Setchell, 1926, and Botryocladia shanksii E.Y.Dawson, 1962." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, seaweeds, reefs, Campeche Bank, Gulf of México, morphology taxonomy" ;
    ecsummary:name "Macroalgae from eight reefs in the Campeche Bank, collected by the National Autonomous University of Mexico (UNAM)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/1de8b1fe-8847-4e4f-9140-cfa6dab91e4c> ;
.

