<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:68da07d9be9a0c6468240bfb3ae2dcc1783cedc7>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The Museum and Art Gallery of the Northern Territory (MAGNT) Coelenterate Collection, established in 1981, consists of about 17,000 databased specimens. The majority of the specimens have been collected from locations in Northern Australia. The collection includes 108 holotypes and 242 paratypes. The collection mainly focuses on shallow water tropical species from the Indo-Pacific, but also includes deep water material from Southern Australia. The collection also includes a small amount of comparative material from the rest of the world.

Specimens can be lent to workers at other institutions upon application and the MAGNT also welcomes visiting researchers.

The collection was established in 1981 and continues to the present.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "Museum and Art Gallery of the Northern Territory Coelenterate Collection, Australia (1924 - 2013)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/e00e2de4-7e7a-4fae-a1da-d3b49aefbf08> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:68e0479c13940423614ab754ab38feca378d145c>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
Mote Marine Laboratory/ Tony Tucker

Dataset credits:
Data provider
Mote Marine Laboratory
Originating data center
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/">Satellite Tracking and Analysis Tool (STAT)</a>
Project partner
Mote Marine Laboratory
Project sponsor or sponsor description
Wooster SchoolPineview Middle SchoolVirginia MillerSarasota Dolphin Research Projecthttp://sarasotadolphin.org


Abstract:
The project has several objectives:1. tracking individuals with long remigration histories2. tracking individuals with original tagging records NOT from Casey Key3. retracking individuals from the oil spill region or Northern Gulf of Mexico.4. retracking individuals from Mexico or the Caribbean.5.tracking individuals with high site fidelity to ensure that datalogger instruments can be recovered.6. Collecting samples for stable isotope, genetic, and trace metal analyses.

Supplemental information:
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/index.shtml?project_id=700">Visit STAT's project page</a> for additional information.

This dataset is a summarized representation of the telemetry locations aggregated per species per 1-degree cell.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Casey Key Loggerheads 2012-2013 (aggregated per 1-degree cell)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/865b16a2-ac9d-4919-95d1-c062ae84823a> ;
.

