<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:6e535db52610d5acced75448635c9f6d46f19c42>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This dataset contains Antarctic Pack Ice seal (APIS) data collected (both ship based and aerial) between 1994 and 2000. This data also includes some historic data collected between 1985 and 1987.  The four species of Antarctic pack ice seals (crabeater, leopard, Weddell, and Ross seals) are thought to comprise up to 50 percent or more of the world's total biomass of seals. As long-lived, top level predators in Southern Ocean ecosystems, pack ice seals are scientifically interesting because they can assist in monitoring shifts in ecosystem structure and function, especially changes that occur in sensitive polar areas in response to global climate changes." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "APIS - Antarctic Pack Ice Seals 1994-1999, plus historical data from the 1980s" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/7e92433a-d086-4527-ab2b-3af86bcbd083> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:6e573b028df5033786ccb9cd6b52bff2a74e1461>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Este conjunto de datos contiene a los artrópodos no Insectos marinos de las Colecciones Biológicas adscritas al Centro de Colecciones Científicas (CCC) de la Universidad del Magdalena. El recurso cuenta con 565 registros de artrópodos marinos, todos provenientes de diferentes sitios del Caribe colombiano, incluyendo la zona costera y de mar abierto. Los especímenes están depositados bajo el acrónimo CBUMAG: ART.
La colección fue documentada, digitalizada y publicada por primera vez durante la ejecución del proyecto BID-CA2020-055-NAC "Incremento de la accesibilidad de información marina de las Colecciones de Historia Natural de Colombia, mediante la movilización de datos, el fortalecimiento de la infraestructura y el entrenamiento". El presente conjunto de datos es el producto de dicho proceso realizado entre 2021-07-01 y 2023-06-30, como parte del entregable “Colección de biología marina del Centro de Colecciones Biológicas de la Universidad del Magdalena – CBUMAG” aportado por la UniMagdalena al proyecto.
This data set contains marine non-insect arthropods from the Biological Collections attached to the Center for Scientific Collections (CCC) of the Universidad del Magdalena. The resource has 565 records of marine arthropods, all from different sites in the Colombian Caribbean, including the coastal zone and the open sea. The specimens are deposited under the acronym CBUMAG: ART.
The collection was documented, digitized and published for the first time during the execution of the BID-CA2020-055-NAC project "Increasing the accessibility of marine information of the Natural History Collections of Colombia, through data mobilization, infrastructure strengthening and training". The present dataset is the product of that process carried out between 2021-07-01 and 2023-06-30, as part of the deliverable "Marine Biology Collection of the Biological Collections Center of the University of Magdalena - CBUMAG" contributed by UniMagdalena to the project.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Specimen, CBUMAG, Arthropoda, Caribe colombiano, marino" ;
    ecsummary:name "Artrópodos no Insectos de las Colecciones Biológicas de la Universidad del Magdalena" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/79511c09-9498-43ad-a7d5-a733b9da3be8> ;
.

