<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:7080c6eef10e6f2e94696ff7cef57c2313cbd86d>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
HDR Environmental, Operations and Construction, Inc.

Dataset credits:
The U.S. Navy Marine Species Monitoring Program

Abstract:
This dataset presents a Guam subset of the results of the Guam and Saipan Marine Species Monitoring: Winter-Spring Survey conducted on the motor vessel (M/V) Sea Fantasy (Guam survey) and the M/V Super Emerald (Saipan survey) from 15 to 29 March 2012.
The objective of the 2012 survey effort was to conduct baseline surveys to further document marine mammal and sea turtle occurrence in nearshore waters around the island of Guam and Saipan. The approach primarily followed opportunistic survey protocols used in recent surveys around Guam (Ligon et al. 2011; HDR 2011), which remained within 10 kilometers (km) or 5.4 nautical miles (NM) of the coastline.

Purpose:
not provided

Supplemental information:
A Saipan subset of the survey is found at <a href=""></a>""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Mariana Islands Range Complex,Vessels,Sightings, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "MIRC Guam Marine Species Monitoring Winter-Spring Surveys 2012" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/b948530a-2dc6-4c64-ace0-c24072787349> ;
.

