<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:7617e96ab7783f6b40e232be974874e1016c7daa>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
HDR Environmental, Operations and Construction, Inc.

Dataset credits:
The U.S. Navy Marine Species Monitoring Program

Abstract:
Aerial surveys for marine-species monitoring occurred during 27 April through 02 May 2013 for an AN/AQS-20 (Q-20) sonar system test event. These surveys were conducted off the west coast of Florida in the Naval Surface Warfare Center Panama City Division (NSWC PCD) Study Area in the Gulf of Mexico. The Q-20 is a high-frequency active sonar (HFAS) system used in mine detection and countermeasures.

Purpose:
U.S. Navy protected marine species monitoring during Q-20 sonar testing""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Navy project,Aircraft,Sightings, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "Sightings for AN/AQS-20 Sonar Test Event - April-May 2013" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/331e31eb-d025-4407-bd22-432b4cfbc936> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:761c11977aa1011ccbedf3e7167001ac6206dbd8>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Processes during the meroplanktonic phase regulate population dynamics for many marine benthic invertebrates. A Canadian Healthy Oceans Network population connectivity project examined changes in vertical distribution of different meroplanktonic larvae in a coastal embayment during a stable period, at high temporal frequencies and spatial resolutions. Meroplanktonic invertebrate larvae (Margarites spp., Crepidula spp., Astyris lunata, Diaphana minuta, Littorinimorpha,  Arrhoges occidentalis, lyanassa spp., Bittiolum  alternatum, Nudibranchia, Gastropods, Bivalves, Bryozoans, Brachyurans, Polychaetes, Carideans, and Asteroids) were collected off a boat at 6 depths (3, 6, 9, 12, 18, 24 m) using a pump, every 2-h over a 36-h (6-7 Aug 2009) and a 25-h (12-13 Aug 2009) period, during a spring and neap tide respectively, concurrently with measures of temperature, salinity, fluorescence and current velocity in St. George's Bay, NS, Canada." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Vertical migration, Temperature, Fluorescence, Lunar phase, Diel period, Tidal state, Water column structure, stratification, Larval behavior, Larval transport, Biophysical model parameter, Abundance, Meroplankton, Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "CHONe: Meroplanktonic larvae from St. George's Bay. A Canadian Healthy Oceans Network population connectivity project" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/357e9435-8b35-4ca9-a674-d3df0b32f0d0> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:761f38dbe97bcf47151f8768297893d87009436b>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Hatakejima Experimental Field is located in Tanabe Bay, Wakayama Prefecture, Japan, which is composed of Hatakejima Island and Komarujima Islet, connected to the former in low tide. Hatakejima Island was purchased by Kyoto University and was designated as the ‘Hatakejima Experimental Field’ in 1968. The long-term surveys have been formally conducted on the experimental field since 1969 as the Century of Research Project. In the entire coast survey, the whole area of the experimental field was subdivided into 43 plots, and presence and absence and relative abundance of selected species of intertidal invertebrates were recorded. This dataset is the result of the entire coast survey conducted from 1983." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "The entire coast survey of Hatakejima Islands from 1983" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/c5f0846d-a31c-4e4d-b1d2-6da882f23694> ;
.

