<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:8d585069ab68b53bf10fb70c43504c229f221e94>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Here we pilot a novel, rapid and non-invasive environmental DNA (eDNA) metabarcoding approach specifically targeted to infer shark presence, diversity and eDNA read abundance in tropical habitats. We identified at least 21 shark species, from both Caribbean and Pacific Coral Sea water samples, whose geographical patterns of diversity and read abundance coincide with geographical differences in levels of anthropogenic pressure and conservation effort. We demonstrate that eDNA metabarcoding can be effectively employed to study shark diversity." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, COI" ;
    ecsummary:name "Environmental DNA reveals tropical shark diversity in contrasting levels of anthropogenic impact" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/dbb57c74-c34c-4502-b1d0-15324a7fabc4> ;
.

