<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:9c0a6d998191a8c9412817bda4ab17e799546085>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
NOAA Northeast Fisheries Science Center (NEFSC)

Dataset credits:
National Marine Fisheries Service

Abstract:
The cruise period was from 06 August - 07 September 1995. The area of operation was Georges Bank and waters east of Cape Cod.

Purpose:
The primary objectives of the survey were to: (1) conduct line-transect population surveys within the study area, and (2) investigate cetacean distribution on the southern portion of Georges Bank, principally between the 30 f isobath and 10 nm beyond the 1000 f curve. Secondary objectives included: (1) collecting information on the relationship cetaceans and oceanographic features, (2) the collection of CTD and zooplankton data, (3) conducting marine mammal photographic
identification studies using a rigid bottom inflatable boat and (4) collecting biopsy samples for stock identification and contaminant studies.

Supplemental information:
In addition to the sighting data, effort data was recorded  every half hour or whenever conditions change.
This dataset, therefore, should be used with the effort data.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Marine Animal Survey,Marine Biology,Marine mammals,Sea turtles,Vessel,Visual Sighting, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "NEFSC 1995 pe9502" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/6843a3c1-b52d-4914-bd2f-b87adfbab2ca> ;
.

