<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:9d5ca62c401d0e09f45e21472187db038a1464a6>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Los siguientes registros biológicos incluyen 603 cangrejos ermitaños pertenecientes a 28 especies del Mar Caribe colombiano que hacen parte del material colectado por las expediciones INVEMAR-Macrofauna I y II, entre 1998 - 2000 y el Proyecto Corpoguajira durante 2005. Estas campañas hacen parte del esfuerzo que se ha llevado a cabo por el Instituto de Investigaciones Marinas y Costeras “José Benito Vives de Andreis” (INVEMAR) a través de las últimas décadas, con el fin de complementar la información sobre la diversidad marina. Los registros aquí contenidos incluyen datos de colecta como la ecorregión (INVEMAR, 2000), lugar, latitud, longitud y profundidad de la zona de captura; información del proceso de conservación y almacenamiento; métodos de muestreo y cruceros relacionados con la captura.
Los códigos de identificación, permiten correlacionar esta base de datos con el material físico del Museo de Historia Natural Marina de Colombia "MAKURIWA" y con el nombre del investigador que identificó la especie. Adicionalmente se incluyen registros de los atributos biológicos de los individuos, tales como longitud y ancho del escudo del caparazón; sexo; número de huevos de las hembras ovadas y diámetro promedio de los huevos de cada nidada; así como la incidencia de parasitismo y el tipo de parásitos encontrados. Permite vincular los registros con publicaciones que los mencionan, así como con fotografías que hacen parte de la colección del Museo de Historia Natural Marina de Colombia "MAKURIWA", descargadas sobre la plataforma Flikr. Esta iniciativa es una primera entrega de la información biológica que será registrada en el “Catálogo de cangrejos ermitaños del mar Caribe colombiano” que se encuentra en proceso de publicación actualmente.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Cangrejos ermitaños; Paguroidea; Mar Caribe; Colombia, Specimen" ;
    ecsummary:name "Registros preliminares del \"Catálogo de cangrejos ermitaños del mar Caribe colombiano\"" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/85fc9de0-2ac2-43e3-bda9-64ef66044bfb> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:9d66fa09090cef9538e6fcd186b69c6b7e3833d0>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Este recurso contiene los datos de monitoreo de aves realizados en Parque Nacional Natural Sanquianga, que se realizaron de 2012 a 2014 en el mes de febrero. Los muestreos se realizaron en los planos lodosos del parque, cubriendo cuatro municipios del departamento de Nariño. Contiene 10.470 registros de 47 especies de aves." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Monitoreo de Aves en planos lodosos, Parques Nacionales, SIB_MARINO, Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Monitoreo de aves presentes en planos lodosos del Parque Nacional Natural Sanquianga" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/5a09b13c-6bab-431d-8de7-c7def1672b06> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:9d70ebf91e8ee2f93962bd3f53f3f2a5b7f8ae60>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Nukutipipi atoll (5 km2), of volcanic origin 16-17 million years old on the Pitcairn (hot spot) Hereheretue line, presents a land flora and fauna of low diversity but with a Pisonia forest and hundreds of resident red-tailed tropic birds. Nukutipipi suffered from the 1983 hurricanes : destruction of vegetation and motu as well as sand lagoon mollusc populations. The north and south rims present original geomorphological structures. Lagoon without patch reefs reaching the surface is characterised by dome patch reefs all constituted of dead Acropora with few scleractinian and mollusc species, but an important algae coverage. All these characteristics indicate the precariousness on a time scale of such a so tiny atoll, land and marine, with a closed lagoon.
Observations on Nukutipipi atoll which we are reporting were mainly in November 1988 but also previously in August 1982 and July 1986.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Data from: Nukutipipi Atoll, Tuamotu Archipelago; Geomorphology, land and marine flora and fauna and interrelationships" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/e43766f7-1ecc-4908-a089-488dda737695> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:9d71afde5351e628506367f14fb8abad95631a0a>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Bedeque Bay, an estuary in Prince Edward Island, yields a consistently large crop of oysters. In 1967, oyster production throughout Prince Edward Island in general was declining and a benthic survey of the main fishing area in the bay was conducted in order to identify the ecological factors or gradients causing the observed spatial composition of the benthos.

The benthic survey was carried out between July 12th and August 14th, 1967, just following the oyster fishing season. Samples were collected underwater by SCUBA divers using a modified suction dredge. The area enclosed by a 1 m2 quadrat was sampled with the dredge (which was equipped with a 4 mm mesh collecting bag) to a depth of 50 era. Forty four stations, covering most of the estuary, were each sampled by a single quadrat.

Animals were counted and plants recorded by dry weight. Only subjective classifications of sediment type based on field observations were made. These measurements are not part of this version of the dataset.

Species distribution information associated with this study were digitized, standardized and republished as part of the Atlantic Coastal Zone Information Steering Committee (ACZISC) Atlantic Ecosystem Initiative (AEI) funded project “Atlantic Canada’s Biological Data for Ecosystem Planning and Decision-making” and OBIS Canada.

 

""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "biota, oceans, biological classification, Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "MEL: Benthic samples collected by divers with a suction dredge from Bedeque Bay, an estuary in Prince Edward Island, Canada in 1967." ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/ab79cae6-c394-43d3-b770-4bf1ad446fe7> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:9d725d19640d1f949c3ebd8f15004df5ad115cbe>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This dataset describes the abyssal megafaunal annelid morphotypes observed during the two ABYSSLINE cruises (AB01/MV1313 - 2013 and AB02/TN319 - 2015) to the UKSRL polymetallic-nodule exploration contract area (UK-1) and the site EPIRB (~250 km east of the UK-1 area) in the Clarion-Clipperton Zone in the Pacific Ocean. These megafaunal annelids were recorded using ROV and AUV. There appear to be at least 5 distinct morphospecies identified by imagery. This dataset is from the paper: Amon D, Ziegler A, Drazen J, Grischenko A, Leitner A, Lindsay D, Voight J, Wicksten M, Young C, Smith C (2017) Megafauna of the UKSRL exploration contract area and eastern Clarion-Clipperton Zone in the Pacific Ocean: Annelida, Arthropoda, Bryozoa, Chordata, Ctenophora, Mollusca. Biodiversity Data Journal 5: e14598. https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.5.e14598" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence; Deep-sea mining; Polymetallic nodule; Clarion-Clipperton Zone; megafauna; Ctenophora" ;
    ecsummary:name "ABYSSLINE UKSRL Contract Area CCZ Megafauna 2013-2015: Ctenophora" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/b9786aec-1ac1-4803-b8d5-50ca7b9e87b4> ;
.

