<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:b250510f08ff413ddeb025225b886f30bfdfb3d5>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
HDR Environmental, Operations and Construction, Inc.

Dataset credits:
The U.S. Navy Marine Species Monitoring Program

Abstract:
Aerial surveys to monitor marine mammals and sea turtles (MM/ST) were conducted in
conjunction with two training events during the period February 16 to March 5, 2011, including
(a) U.S. Navy Submarine Commander’s Course (SCC) naval training event in the Hawaii Range
Complex (HRC) on the Pacific Missile Range Facility (PMRF) instrumented range between Kauai
and Niihau, Hawaii; and
(b) Undersea Warfare Exercise (USWEX) training event south of Oahu and Molokai.
Surveys in support of the SCC event occurred on 4 consecutive days from February 16 to 19, 2011, in waters adjoining Kauai and Niihau where the missile destroyer (DDG)
and other ships were operating, followed by shoreline surveys of Kauai and Niihau on 2 separate days thereafter: February 24 and 26, 2011.
This was followed by shoreline surveys of the Four
Islands region in support of the USWEX event on 2 separate days, February 28 and March 5, 2011.
The survey methods and sampling design were submitted and approved in advance, per the
statement of work (SOW), to the Navy Technical Representative (NTR) and followed previously
established protocol (Mobley and Milette 2010; Smultea et al. 2009a,b).

Purpose:
not provided

Supplemental information:
[2017-10-13] Data fields are changed so that they follow other Navy datasets.

This dataset includes sightings during the USWEX shoreline surveys.

Sightings during the ship-follow surveys are available:
<a href="http://seamap.env.duke.edu/dataset/922">HRC SCC Aerial-based Shp-follow Surveys  February 2011</a>

Sightings during the transect surveys are available:
<a href="http://seamap.env.duke.edu/dataset/923">HRC SCC Aerial-based Transect Surveys  February 2011</a>

Data for the SCC shoreline surveys are available:
<a href="http://seamap.env.duke.edu/dataset/924">HRC SCC Aerial-based Shoreline Surveys  February 2011</a>""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Hawaii Range Complex,Airplane,Sightings, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "HRC USWEX Aerial-based Shoreline Surveys February and March 2011" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/c0e0900c-d10e-4dac-9b64-7a8927abb2f9> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:b258ed8cca9510f6f50789d131d53bdd110f5227>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This dataset contains a list of the presence, habitats and herbarium vouchers of the species of the Siphonocladales sampled at the Kenyan coast. Field work was carried out on a yearly basis from July 1985 till September 1992. Sampling was done by walking or wading at low tide and by snorkeling at high tide. All algae were collected in separate pots or bags. All specimens were determined with a Reichert light microscope and a Wild stereoscopic binocular. The data were digitized by VLIZ from the original report: Verstraete, H. (1993). De Siphonocladales (Chlorophyta) van de Keniaanse kust. The Siphonocladales (Chlorophyta) of the Kenyan coast.. MSc Thesis. Rijksuniversiteit Gent. Faculteit Wetenschappen: Gent. 90 text, 18 ill. 33 fig. Pp." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "human, Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Siphonocladales (Chlorophyta) sampled at the Kenyan coast between 1985 and 1992" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/47798b3a-6a79-4342-ad75-48a3e7f05a8d> ;
.

