<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:b55da4eeaa179ce5fe7406f4cd79349ea2269e66>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "The Fisheries Logbook System records the fishing and non-fishing activity of fishermen who are required to report their fishing activity via logbooks submitted for each trip. The Southeast Fisheries Science Center (SEFSC) manages two vessel logbook programs. This program principally covers vessels that use pelagic longline gear, but also includes vessels that use other types of gear (harpoon and handline) that target pelagic species in the highly migratory species fishery management plan. This logbook program was initiated in 1986, and has continued uninterrupted since then. Because the pelagic program supports assessments that require catch per unit effort data for individual sets, the design of this program focuses on data for individual sets." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "NOAA Southeast Fisheries Science Center (SEFSC) Fisheries Log Book System (FLS) Commercial Pelagic Logbook Data" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/0ca901d4-bdc3-4136-8a66-6028f4c3ba40> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:b55dc176f56415e1b626a4d5228e20cffba65796>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
NOAA Pacific Islands Fisheries Science Center (PIFSC)

Dataset credits:
NOAA Pacific Islands Fisheries Science Center

Abstract:
The Pacific Islands Cetacean Ecosystem Assessment Survey (PICEAS) was a line-transect survey for cetaceans was conducted within the Palmyra exclusive economic zone (EEZ)(20 October - 18 November 2011). The set of standard tracklines surveyed was established prior to the cruise and was intended to cover approximately two thirds of the Palmyra Atoll EEZ transect line grid used for the 2005 PICEAS (AR-05-07) survey conducted by Southwest Fisheries Science Center. This was the first of two surveys that were designed to cover the entire Palmyra EEZ. Twenty-eight days of on-effort surveys were completed during the cruise, resulting in 28 cetacean sightings including seven identified species and five types of unidentified cetaceans.

Supplemental information:
Data were collected under NMFS permit 14097.
The data included here are the sightings and on-effort tracks recorded within WinCruz survey software and extracted from the QA/QC'd DAS file using the R package swfscDAS (https://smwoodman.github.io/swfscDAS).

Attributes for fields within the trackline files:
Cruise - see description in attribute table below
segnum - segment number for continuous on-effort line
Date - Local date m/dd/yyyy
TimeStart - Local time at start of on-effort segment
LatStart - Latitude in decimal degrees at starting point of on-effort segment
LongStart - Longitude in decimal degrees at starting point of on-effort segment
TimeEnd - Local time at end of on-effort segment
LatEnd - Latitude in decimal degrees at end point of on-effort segment
LongEnd - Longitude in decimal degrees at end point of on-effort segment
Mode - see description in attribute table below
EffType - see description in attribute table below
avgSpdKt - average speed (knots) of the ship over the on-effort segment traveled
avgBft - average Beaufort Sea State over the on-effort segment

Other data not included here:
Photos and biopsy samples were collected during some sightings. There were acoustic detections from the towed hydrophone array. Sonobuoys were deployed opportunistically. A High-frequency Acoustic Recording Package (HARP) was deployed off Kingman Reef. Oceanographic data were collected (CTD, XBT).

See the PIFSC Cetacean Survey, PICEAS 2012, Cruise 1203, NOAA Pacific Islands Fisheries Science Center for cetacean sightings and effort within the remaining portion of the Palmyra EEZ.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Marine Animal Survey,Marine Biology,Marine mammals,Visual Sighting,Vessel, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "PIFSC, Cetacean Survey, PICEAS 2011, Cruise 1108, NOAA Pacific Islands Fisheries Science Center" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/834e5943-f06e-4a91-8ab1-d324b57405d0> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:b57fbb9249b5d4ef6841c5e278f7b0fe044a3d82>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This study was carried out to compare the results of nutrient and phytoplankton measurements in inlets of Prince Edward Island (PEI), in order to look for relationships between species composition and nutrient levels. We also considered the likelihood of nutrient limitation within the phytoplankton community by comparing ambient nutrient concentrations with the inherent ability of the phytoplankton to take up the nutrients at low concentrations." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "BioChem: Prince Edward Island inlet phytoplankton monitoring during late summer to fall, 2001-2003" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/8f72cf3f-5562-4be0-b0ad-c248f4fd211b> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:b584f1278d84fbd28badad948d01e74cfa52c940>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The aim of the Intergovernmental Oceanographic Commission of UNESCO (IOC) Harmful Algal Bloom (HAB) global status report literature search project is to create a reliable verified data set for all toxic HAB taxa by geographic region.  Records within the dataset point to an authoritative source, typically a publication that contains information on occurrence of harmful algae. This literature search is limited to only toxic algae. The full list of harmful algal species (http://www.marinespecies.org/hab/) was beyond the scope of this project. Records are summarized information and include a scientific name, the start and end dates when the taxon was observed and the geographic extent of the observations. The objective was not to create records for individual water samples or net tows that were collected and on which the reference paper was based - these detailed records would all be associated with a specific latitude/longitude and date/time. If the publication provided an exact area definition with latitude and longitude for the geographic extent this information is provided. If only a general place name was provided then a known locality name was assigned by the literature search editor and nominal coordinates assigned. If a harmful algal event was associated with the species occurrence, then a link to the IODE/HAEDAT database is provided.

In summary this resource provides a trustworthy location of an algal taxon that points to a reference paper (literature). This resource contains contributions from HAB project editors searching for content in an area of interest to Colombia. This area was defined as the unofficial EEZ area as defined in the marine regions gazetteer (http://marineregions.org/).

 
/
El objetivo de la Comisión Oceanográfica Intergubernamental de la UNESCO (COI) a través del Programa de Floraciones de Algas Nocivas (FAN), es la creación de un conjunto de datos verificados y fiables para todos los taxones FAN tóxicos por región geográfica. Los registros dentro de la base de datos establecida, son típicamente publicaciones que contienen información sobre la aparición de algas nocivas. Esta búsqueda bibliográfica se limita sólo a las algas tóxicas. La lista completa de las especies de algas nocivas (http://www.marinespecies.org/hab/) fue más allá del alcance de este proyecto. Los registros se resumen de la información e incluye un nombre científico, las fechas de inicio y finalización de los eventos cuando se observó el taxón y la extensión geográfica de las observaciones. El objetivo no era crear registros para las muestras individuales de agua o redes que fueron recogidos y en la que se basa el documento de referencia - estos registros detallados pueden ser asociados a una latitud / longitud específica y fecha / hora. Si la publicación proporcionó una definición de área exacta con la latitud y la longitud de la extensión geográfica se proporciona esta información. Si únicamente se proporcionó el nombre de una localidad, este fue asignado por  la búsqueda en la literatura y se asignaron coordenadas nominales por parte del editor. Si un evento de algas nocivas se asoció con la presencia de especies, se proporciona un enlace a la base de datos del IODE / HAEDAT. 
En resumen este recurso proporciona una ubicación confiable de un taxón de algas con base en un documento de referencia (Bibliografía). Este recurso contiene además la descripción de un área de interés para Colombia. Esta zona se define como un área no oficial de la ZEE tal como se define en la gaceta geográfica sobre regiones marinas.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "HAB Region 2: Occurrences of harmful (toxic) algal taxa within an area of interest to Colombia compiled as part of a literature search project." ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/5a967235-7e1b-4bcd-a1f8-cd185d4bc0f8> ;
.

