    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/5c37fe6f-16d7-4da2-a591-fb4420fc217f> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c931e6e573a6f0dc4579188b9116ecedfdeaf99c>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
International Fund for Animal Welfare

Dataset credits:
International Fund for Animal Welfare

Abstract:
Boat-based acoustic and visual surveys for harbor porpoises (<i>Phocoena phocoena</i>) were conducted during the summers of 2001 and 2002in order to investigate their distribution and relative abundance in the Baltic Sea, and to compare the results with the adjacent Kiel and Mecklenburg Bights and the Little Belt.

Purpose:
Harbor porpoises are subject to year-round bycatch in gillnets and other fishing gear in these waters. This is of particular concern in the Baltic Sea where a survey carried out in 1995 indicated that the population is low and current levels of anthropogenic mortality are believed to be unsustainable.

Supplemental information:
6/15/2010: The primary contact was changed from Douglas Gillespie to Anna Moscrop upon provider request.



3/28/2007: _obs_count (species count) field was blank. It is now filled with proper counts.



This dataset includes visual sightings events only.
Data for acoustic events during the survey are available in Baltic Porpoise Acoustic Surveys 01-02.
Acoustic sound files are not available in OBIS-SEAMAP.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Marine mammals,Habor porpoise,Habour porpoise,Acoustic survey,Visual survey, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "Baltic Porpoise Sightings 01-02" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/fabd272c-df1a-4ffb-9ecc-9af1a17bc27a> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c93a1f955708f8cbd60d510357c95431da8660a8>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """This voyage was used to test and refine optimal techniques to map and assess seabed habitat. The sampling locations are a number of submarine canyons and their immediately adjacent flanks on the west coast of Tasmania and east of Bass Strait.
Taxa have been matched to the World Register of Marine Species (WoRMS). Reports, metadata and other data from this voyage are at https://www.marine.csiro.au/data/trawler/survey_details,cfm?survey=SS200404""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Specimen" ;
    ecsummary:name "CSIRO, Cruise SS200404, Benthic Biodiversity, Tasmanian Coast; Bass Strait; Tasman Sea; NSW Coast, 2004" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/72f00c0d-996a-4191-8b45-e701f75da0d1> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c93c115e8be8a5fee7f968a3edee34f213d80001>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Este recurso es producto de la caracterización de la megafauna bentónica y demersal de la Cresta Beata realizada entre 2021 y 2022 por el Invemar, en acuerdo con el Ministerio de Ambiente y Desarrollo Sostenible de Colombia como insumo para la declaratoria del área como Reserva Natural (Categoria I de la UICN). El conjunto de datos incluye 432 registros de especies de fauna profunda, obtenidas a partir de las imágenes capturadas en video y fotografía por un vehículo de operación remota (R.O.V), mediante transectos realizados a través de la Cresta Beata entre los 1641 y 3000 m de profundidad. La identificación del material visual, fue llevada a cabo por especialistas nacionales reconocidos para los diferentes grupos y corroborada por expertos internacionales. Del total de especies reportadas el 42% corresponden a Equinodermos, 20% a cnidarios, 18% a esponjas, 11% a crustáceos, 6% a peces, 2% a moluscos, 1% son anélidos y 0.2% ctenóforos. Asociado al conjunto de datos también se incluye la información multimedia de 119 fotografías aportadas como evidencia de las ocurrencias, la cual se detalla en la extensión SimpleMultimedia. Las imágenes forman parte de la Colección Digital Catálogo de Fauna de Profundidad (CFP) del Museo de Historia Natural Marina de Colombia Makuriwa (MHNMC).


""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "occurrence, Specimen, Caribe colombiano, Cresta Beata, Biodiversidad marina, Comunidades de profundidad, Crucero de Investigación Cordillera Submarina Beata, Peces, Cnidaria, Crustacea, Ctenophora, Echinodermata, Mollusca, Porifera, Annelida" ;
    ecsummary:name "Caracterización de la fauna epibentónica y demersal de la Reserva Natural Cordillera Beata" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/99e432a3-9be6-4374-b6d2-91e29d6a5987> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c93e4930715189fddac82365ed5122ec6546e63e>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
University of Rhode Island

Dataset credits:
University of Rhode Island
Bureau of Land Management
U.S. Dept of the Interior

Abstract:
The Cetacean and Turtle Assessment Program (CETAP) was sponsored by the Bureau of Land Management and conducted between October 1978 and January 1982 by the University of Rhode Island in outer continental shelf waters of the northeastern United States from Cape Hatteras, North Carolina, to the Gulf of Maine and from shore to 9.3 km (5 nautical miles) seaward of the 1829 m (1,000 fathoms) isobath. Population surveys were conducted by CETAP to assess the distribution and abundance of whales, dolphins and sea turtles inhabiting the study area.

Purpose:
This dataset is a subset of CETAP_AIR extracting animal sighting records with taxonomic information of species sighted added. The full dataset may be available upon request. Please contact the primary contact person for the proper use of the dataset.

Supplemental information:
[2020-09-30] The following invalid species names were corrected according to the Integrated Taxonomic Information System (ITIS).
Turtles: Testudines (173749) =&gt; Testudines (948936)

Metadata are currently being revised. Sighting points that were more than 2 km inland were eliminated. Those from 1 km to 2 km inland can be considered as on-water sightings. Those records have TRUE in the [Excluded] field to indicate that they seem to fall on land but may be correct sightings.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Marine Animal Survey,Marine Biology,Marine mammals,Sea turtles,Aircraft,Visual Sighting, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "BLM CETAP AIR Sightings" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/6669ce88-d264-42a5-b34c-bb7f01c3952c> ;
.

