<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c986e7fcf7b3a1a123ba14f52d655c277da1b16b>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "The dataset contains information on specimens examined in the paper “An update on marine sponge diversity in the Southern Gulf of Mexico coral reefs” submitted in Zootaxa. This dataset contains information on 231 specimens of 80 species of the Demospongiae class, including their distribution in coral reefs in the Southern Gulf of Mexico, and their depth. All specimens are hosted in the National Collection of the Phylum Porifera Gerardo Green” (CNPGG), at the Instituto de Ciencias del Mar y Limnología, Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México, Mexico City." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Gulf of Mexico, Campeche Bank, Coral Reefs, Porifera" ;
    ecsummary:name "Porifera diversity and distribution data in the Southern Gulf of Mexico" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/5acccdb9-8230-4ec7-bea0-5bf3b0ce9d70> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c98af1ef670d0734a00f2230ebe40498104254ab>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "El Cayo Bolívar o Cayos del Este-sureste es un atolón del mar Caribe que se encuentra ubicado en la tercera sección, en la parte sur (14.780 km2) de la reserva de biosfera Seaflower. Durante la expedición científica realizada en esta localidad (2022), se registró la fauna íctica asociada a los diferentes ecosistemas encontrados, los cuales incluyen fondos arenosos, pastos marinos, arrecifes coralinos y rocosos. Para el registro de las especies ícticas asociadas a esta localidad, se implementó la metodología de censo visual a través de buceo autónomo diurno, en 20 puntos de muestreo alrededor del cayo. La profundidad muestreada estuvo en un rango entre los 1,5 m y los 40 m. Adicionalmente, se colectaron 19 ejemplares de Microspathodon chrysurus, a los cuales se les tomó una muestra de tejido para posteriores análisis moleculares. Con los datos y muestras obtenidas en esta localidad se completa la zona sur de la reserva. Esto permitirá explorar la relación entre diversidad específica con la edad y tamaño de la isla e inferir sobre el grado de similitud entre la diversidad taxonómica y funcional de islas oceánicas." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "ROV, Aguas profundas, Samplingevent" ;
    ecsummary:name "Microspathodon chrysurus observados en la Expedición Seaflower Isla Cayo Bolivar 2022 - Proyecto Colombia BIO" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/69043aaf-751b-4bf0-9325-a99e719f4b61> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c99522520a43d2a838d90cc334fdc7eac7443528>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """In January 2019, the governments of Chile and Argentina, in collaboration with National Geographic Pristine Seas, organized an expedition to the Antarctic Peninsula, with the aim to provide political, scientific, and communication support, at a global scale, to the Marine Protected Area proposal for the Antarctic Peninsula-South Scotia Arc (Domain 1 MPA or D1MPA) that was put forward jointly by the two countries in October 2018. To this end, they set out to explore the ecosystems of the continental shelf along the  WAP and associated islands using National Geographic’s deep-sea cameras to capture high  quality imagery of areas of the Antarctic sea floor and the associated fauna, which have been  comparatively less well explored.
This bi-national expedition was conducted on the Chilean Navy vessel, the OPV-83 Marinero Fuentealba, with scientists from both countries national Antarctic Institutes. 
In order to study the continental shelf faunal biodiversity of Antarctica , baited  cameras were deployed at 20 locations along ~ 500 km of the Western Antarctic Peninsula (WAP) at depths from 90 to 797 m.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Argentina–Chile National Geographic Pristine Seas Expedition To The Antarctic Peninsula - Deep Sea Cam Data" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/7afba27f-8547-4899-829e-b4bd25765322> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c9a5e3a97be3fa94ddcdb171f1e20e9c98172a29>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This dataset provides information on fishes of the northern Gulf of St. Lawrence ecosystem. Diverse sources in Quebec have been consulted from the literature (1933-2012) and from biological surveys (1997-2012) conducted by the Department of Fisheries and Oceans Canada (DFO) Quebec Region and its partners. The habitats covered are principally from offshore surveys, though it includes shore-based surveys, particularly of intertidal eelgrass beds as well as intertidal marshes and mud flats of the middle and lower portion of the St. Lawrence estuary. The data has been compiled into a geodatabase with environmental information on sites and biological information on most specimens. This dataset provides only the abundance and gender of specimens recorded in the database from the total of 664799 individual records with 185 taxa at 5243 sites. The records have been checked for taxonomic and geographic reliability. The dataset provides a comprehensive overview of fish records for the St. Lawrence region as a complement to published survey datasets. / Cet ensemble de données fournit des informations sur les poissons de l'écosystème du nord du golfe du Saint-Laurent. Des sources diverses au Québec ont été consultés à partir de la littérature (1933-2012) et de relevés biologiques (1997-2012) faits par le Ministère de Pêches et Océans Canada (MPO) de la région du Québec et ses partenaires. Les habitats considérés comprennent notamment des milieux de haute mer, mais aussi des sites littoraux, en particulier des herbiers de zostères, des marais à spartine et des vasières intertidales. Les données ont été compilées dans une géodatabase incluant des informations environnementales sur les sites et des informations biologiques sur une grande proportion des spécimens capturés. Cet ensemble de données est une compilation par espèce, par sexe et par stationdes 664799 enregistrements individuels dans la base de données qui compte un total de 185 taxa répartis entre 5243 sites. La validité taxonomique et géographique des enregistrements a été vérifiée. Cet ensemble de données fournit un aperçu global de l’information concernant les poissons du Saint-Laurent, constituant un complément aux données déjà publiées.." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Northwest Atlantic; Estuarine; Marine; Pisces; Distribution; Monitoring; Historical; Biodiversity; Ecological niche modelling; Deep water, Biological classification; Oceans;, Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Northern Gulf of St. Lawrence Fishes" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/18e4fa5b-5f92-4e09-957b-b242003287e9> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c9a9b6d22af5f6329607b6a5bad75f711c7a2301>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Record fauna observational summary data within the N.T. Taxonomic and collection data for observed mammals, birds, reptiles, frogs. Includes presence/absence info, date, time, and location of sighting. Data collected after 1995 may also include counts.
Records were downloaded from the Atlas of Living Australia (https://collections.ala.org.au/public/show/dr361). Taxa have been matched to the World Register of Marine Species. Non-marine records based on that register have been excluded from this version.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Fauna Atlas N.T. - marine records, Northern Territory, Australia" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/81052564-3563-4036-9031-872cb056e936> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c9ac03f244bd5f928dbd25944d169e427e718662>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """The aim of the Intergovernmental Oceanographic Commission of UNESCO (IOC) Harmful Algal Bloom (HAB) global status report literature search project is to create a reliable verified data set for all toxic HAB taxa by geographic region.  Records within the dataset point to an authoritative source, typically a publication that contains information on occurrence of harmful algae. This literature search is limited to only toxic algae. The full list of harmful algal species (http://www.marinespecies.org/hab/) was beyond the scope of this project. Records are summarized information and include a scientific name, the start and end dates when the taxon was observed and the geographic extent of the observations. The objective was not to create records for individual water samples or net tows that were collected and on which the reference paper was based - these detailed records would all be associated with a specific latitude/longitude and date/time. If the publication provided an exact area definition with latitude and longitude for the geographic extent this information is provided. If only a general place name was provided then a known locality name was assigned by the literature search editor and nominal coordinates assigned. If a harmful algal event was associated with the species occurrence, then a link to the IODE/HAEDAT database is provided.

In summary this resource provides a trustworthy location of an algal taxon that points to a reference paper (literature). This resource contains contributions from HAB project editors searching for content in an area of interest to Nicaragua. This area was defined as the unofficial EEZ area as defined in the marine regions gazetteer (http://marineregions.org/).

 
/
El objetivo de la Comisión Oceanográfica Intergubernamental de la UNESCO (COI) a través del Programa de Floraciones de Algas Nocivas (FAN), es la creación de un conjunto de datos verificados y fiables para todos los taxones FAN tóxicos por región geográfica. Los registros dentro de la base de datos establecida, son típicamente publicaciones que contienen información sobre la aparición de algas nocivas. Esta búsqueda bibliográfica se limita sólo a las algas tóxicas. La lista completa de las especies de algas nocivas (http://www.marinespecies.org/hab/) fue más allá del alcance de este proyecto. Los registros se resumen de la información e incluye un nombre científico, las fechas de inicio y finalización de los eventos cuando se observó el taxón y la extensión geográfica de las observaciones. El objetivo no era crear registros para las muestras individuales de agua o redes que fueron recogidos y en la que se basa el documento de referencia - estos registros detallados pueden ser asociados a una latitud / longitud específica y fecha / hora. Si la publicación proporcionó una definición de área exacta con la latitud y la longitud de la extensión geográfica se proporciona esta información. Si únicamente se proporcionó el nombre de una localidad, este fue asignado por  la búsqueda en la literatura y se asignaron coordenadas nominales por parte del editor. Si un evento de algas nocivas se asoció con la presencia de especies, se proporciona un enlace a la base de datos del IODE / HAEDAT. 
En resumen este recurso proporciona una ubicación confiable de un taxón de algas con base en un documento de referencia (Bibliografía). Este recurso contiene además la descripción de un área de interés para Nicaragua. Esta zona se define como un área no oficial de la ZEE tal como se define en la gaceta geográfica sobre regiones marinas.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Specimen" ;
    ecsummary:name "HAB Region 2: Occurrences of harmful (toxic) algal taxa within an area of interest to Nicaragua compiled as part of a literature search project." ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/042dd549-775a-4441-ac7b-02c715497daa> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:c9aca83ca3f8ffae8f593983b44aefaab064b267>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Stomach content data of steelhead trout (O. mykiss) caught in the North Pacific Ocean. This dataset is an aggregation of several capture events between 1994 and 2009. These data were extracted and aggregated by Caroline Graham, Evgeny A. Pakhomov and Brian P. V. Hunt as part of a larger database project: the North Pacific Marine Salmon Diet Database (NPMSDD). Further information on the NPMSDD is provided here: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-020-00676-y. The dynamic GitHub repository can be found here: https://github.com/mcarolinegraham/North_Pacific_Marine_Salmon_Diet_Database." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Metadata" ;
    ecsummary:name "Stomach contents of steelhead trout (Oncorhynchus mykiss) caught in the North Pacific Ocean - 1994 to 2009" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/422c3f13-db22-4bb0-b9bd-98d09ac2f6ab> ;
.

