<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:dc30000df9dcffebd3a89057f7f5e87d30672119>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
University of Rhode Island

Dataset credits:
University of Rhode Island
Bureau of Land Management
US Dept of the Interior

Abstract:
The Cetacean and Turtle Assessment Program (CETAP) was sponsored by the Bureau of Land Management and conducted between October 1978 and January 1982 by the University of Rhode Island in outer continental shelf  waters of the northeastern United States from Cape Hatteras, North Carolina, to the Gulf of Maine and from shore to 9.3 km (5 nautical miles) seaward of the 1829 m (1000 fathoms) isobath. Population surveys were conducted by CETAP to assess the distribution and abundance of whales, dolphins and sea turtles inhabiting the study area.

Supplemental information:
[2020-09-30] The following invalid species names were corrected according to the Integrated Taxonomic Information System (ITIS).
Turtles: Testudines (173749) =&gt; Testudines (948936)

This dataset is a subset of CETAP sightings, extracting opportunistic sighting records, with the addition of taxonomic information of species sighted. The full dataset may be available upon request. Requests for more data, further details on the dataset, proper use of the dataset, and questions should be directed to the primary contact person.

Also note that the metadata is in edits. For further details of the dataset or questions, contact the contact person.

Sighting points that are more than 2km inland were eliminated.
Those from 1km to 2km inland can be considered as on-water sightings.

Accuracy of date/time varies. See tprecision field.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Marine Animal Survey,Marine Biology,Marine mammals,Sea turtles,Aircraft,Visual Sighting, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "BLM CETAP OPP Sightings" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/ac41ae6d-b990-4656-b943-3c978bd2922c> ;
.

