<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:e14a95d58b1de660c7946987d7a67d6326138b1f>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """This dataset includes measured fluxes of phytoplankton cells, total particulate matter, chloropigments, particulate organic carbon, and particulate nitrogen, as well as carbon and nitrogen isotopic signatures on samples from moored sediment traps deployed offshore Pointe-des-Monts and Baie-Comeau. The sediment trap cups were programmed to rotate approximately every two weeks from November 2020 to September 2021. Offshore Pointe-des-Monts, sinking particles were collected at depths of 154 and 224 m while offshore Baie-Comeau, sinking particles were collected at a depth of 133 m. The objective of this work is to understand the influence of an active submarine canyon system on biogenic matter export fluxes. This project was funded by Réseau Québec Maritime (RQM) and Marine Environmental Observation, Prediction, and Response Network (MEOPAR).
Ce jeu de données comprend les flux mesurés de cellules phytoplanctoniques, de matières particulaires totales, de chloropigments, de carbone organique particulaire et d'azote particulaire, ainsi que les signatures isotopiques du carbone et de l'azote sur des échantillons provenant de pièges à sédiments déployés au large de Pointe-des-Monts et de Baie-Comeau. Les bouteilles des pièges à sédiments étaient programmées pour une rotation environ toutes les deux semaines de novembre 2020 à septembre 2021. Au large de Pointe-des-Monts, les particules ont été collectées à des profondeurs de 154 et 224 m tandis qu'au large de Baie-Comeau, les particules ont été collectées à une profondeur de 133 m dans la colonne d’eau. L'objectif de ce travail est de comprendre l'influence d'un système de canyons sous-marins actifs sur les flux d'exportation de matière biogénique. Ce projet a été financé par le Réseau Québec Maritime (RQM) et le Marine Environmental Observation, Prediction, and Response Network (MEOPAR).""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Samplingevent, Stable carbon isotopes, Particulate matter, Phytoplankton biomass and diversity | Isotopes stables du carbone, Matière particulaire, Biomasse et diversité de phytoplancton, chlorophyll a, phytoplankton, Pointe-des-Monts, Baie-Comeau, particulate matter, sediment traps | chlorophylle a, phytoplancton, matières particulaires, pièges à sediments" ;
    ecsummary:name "Time-Series Biogenic Matter Export Fluxes Offshore Pointe-des-Monts and Baie-Comeau | Flux de matière biogénique au large de Pointe-des-Monts et de Baie-Comeau" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/9228a6df-b054-4323-9858-027d7961959b> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:e14b67206f5ada245ff8ba2056592fb298a3ea0a>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
Qld Department of Environment and Heritage Protection

Dataset credits:
Data provider
GHD, Xstrata and  DERM nesting flatback monitoring
Originating data center
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/">Satellite Tracking and Analysis Tool (STAT)</a>


Abstract:
Little is known of the inter-nesting and feeding habitat used by flatback turtles nesting on the northern part of Cape York Peninsula.  This project is part of a state-wide turtle and dugong awareness program designed to shed light on where the feeding areas are for these turtles.Apudthama Rangers named their turtles ‘Kiku’ and 'Cecilia'.Kiku and Cecilia laid their eggs on Jardine River beach at approximately 7.30pm on 12 September 2014. Upon finishing laying they were intercepted by the Apudthama rangers and taken back to camp for satellite transmitter attachment, assessment and sampling.They were also tagged with both titanium tags and pit tags for future identification and mark recapture analysis. They both appeared to be in good health.Kiku and Cecilia were successfully released and watched from the beach by Rangers as they swam towards the horizon, hopefully to return again soon to nest or shed light on their migration pathways and feeding areas.

Supplemental information:
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/index.shtml?project_id=1046">Visit STAT's project page</a> for additional information.

This dataset is a summarized representation of the telemetry locations aggregated per species per 1-degree cell.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Apudthama Ranger flatback tracking project (aggregated per 1-degree cell)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/e990dc5f-d7ae-4eff-b6da-f096bedbe50a> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:e14c9e0813541f3c9d68557857e15dea45594b63>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "Pacific Salmon Foundation (PSF) dataset on marine microalgae (20-200 µm) that are known or suspected to have a negative effect on aquaculture (finfish, shellfish) based on ~bi-monthly sampling (up to 20 times a year) from ~55 sampling sites in the Strait of Georgia, Canada. Samples were analyzed on a Sedgewick-Rafter slide; the identification of specimens was done to the lowest taxonomic level possible and the enumeration (as cells mL-1) by a taxonomist certified by Intergovernmental Oceanographic Commission (IOC) in Proficiency in Identification of Harmful Algae." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Samplingevent, latitude, longitude, depth, phytoplankton, occurrence, algae, oceanography" ;
    ecsummary:name "Harmful Algae in the Strait of Georgia, 2015-2023" ;
