.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:e5f32baaf0d604c2e95fa5438fff223849b18d2b>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
Coastal Research and Education Society of Long Island, Inc.

Dataset credits:
Coastal Research and Education Society of Long Island, Inc.

Abstract:
Cetacean sightings data for the waters off Montauk for July through early 
September 2022

Purpose:
The Coastal Research and Education Society of Long Island is a non-profit 
research and education organization. Our mission is: "To promote and 
foster 
understanding and stewardship of coastal ecosystems through research 
and 
education ." Part of our work is to observe, document, and collect pertinent 
data and photographs of  the whale and sea bird populations of NY and 
New England and to take people to see these animals in the wild.

Since 1996 we have been offering incredible and successful single day and 
multi-day offshore pelagic bird and whale observation trips.

Supplemental information:
A static view of vessel tracks is available. To show it online, go to "Layers" tab 
and choose "Vessel tracks".""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,Marine Animal Survey,Marine Biology,Marine mammals,Visual Sighting,Vessel, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "CRESLI marine mammal observations from whale watch cruises 2022" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/02e343a2-d532-40f3-9402-d223d9fbab6f> ;
.

