<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:e618ab475638f6a4692c3f8101e0074b8f41dacc>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
North Carolina Aquariums

Dataset credits:
Data provider
NC Aquariums Cold Stunned Sea Turtle Monitoring
Originating data center
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/">Satellite Tracking and Analysis Tool (STAT)</a>
Project sponsor or sponsor description
This project is supported by the Triad Foundation


Abstract:
Every year, cold-stunned sea turtles strand on North Carolina beaches.  Rehabilitation centers, including the North Carolina Aquariums, assist the rescue effort by providing care and returning these animals to good health.  These turtles are then released offshore into the warm waters of the Gulf Stream, and this project aims to understand where young green turtles go and how they fare in this environment after recovering from cold stunning.

Supplemental information:
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/index.shtml?project_id=705">Visit STAT's project page</a> for additional information.

This dataset is a summarized representation of the telemetry locations aggregated per species per 1-degree cell.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "NC Aquariums Cold Stunned Sea Turtle Monitoring (aggregated per 1-degree cell)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/1bc1fe8f-4485-4342-92a0-b87d61b7e826> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:e618cf2657571f99992120c4814d8bea45a29b96>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Fisheries oriented inventory that consists of tabular information and an atlas of estuarine wetlands describing 133 estuaries and embayments along the NSW (Australia) coast. Vegetation-types identified on these maps were saltmarshes (all species combined), mangroves (all species combined), and seagrasses. In the case of seagrasses, the following species or families were mapped: Zosteraceae (including Zostera capricorni, Zostera muelleri, and Heterozostera tasmanica), Posidonia australis, Halophila spp. (Halophila ova/is and Halophila decipiens) and Ruppia spp. (Ruppia megacarpa, Ruppia polycarpa and Ruppia maritima).
This dataset is hosted by the Institute for Marine and Antarctic Studies (IMAS), University of Tasmania, on behalf of the NSW Office of Environment and Heritage, New South Wales Government for the purposes of Seamap Australia (testing a national marine benthic habitat classification scheme). Data and metadta sourced from https://metadata.imas.utas.edu.au/geonetwork/srv/eng/metadata.show?uuid=021f65eb-38c6-4db2-9dbe-821b6b427780""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "An Estuarine Inventory for New South Wales, Australia" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/c1181498-9389-4962-b98b-bf5d7a5fb7cd> ;
.

