<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:e6808218c0fa8d6fb6dd2958bcb8699ef9415ef9>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """DSC-RTP Database Version 20241022-1
NOAA’s Deep-Sea Coral Research and Technology Program (DSC-RTP) has compiled national database of the known locations of deep-sea corals and sponges in U.S. territorial waters and beyond. The database is comprehensive, standardized, quality controlled, and networked to outside resources. The database schema accommodates both linear (trawls, transects) and point (samples, observations) data. The structure of the database is tailored to occurrence records of all the azooxanthellate corals, a subset of all corals, and all sponge species. Fish records are also included when annotated along with coral coral and sponge occurrences. Records shallower than 50 m are generally excluded in order to focus on predominantly deep-water species – the mandate of the DSC-RTP. The intention is to limit the overlap with light-dependent (and mostly shallow-water) corals. To query, visualize, and download data in its native format, please visit our map portal: 
https://ncei.noaa.gov/maps/deep-sea-corals-portal/mapSites.htm For advanced data query and data download, please visit our ERDDAP data access form:  
https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/erddap/tabledap/deep_sea_corals.html 

To learn more about NOAA's National Database for Deep-Sea Corals and Sponges, visit our website: 
https://deepseacoraldata.noaa.gov/data""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "NOAA Deep-Sea Coral Research and Technology Program" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/f5a4799e-dc24-4807-89d9-01da47d52e3b> ;
.

