<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:efaa0d7baa8e36a53120648c45e1dfaef5ce6b2d>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "The dataset contains information on specimens examined in the paper “An update on marine sponge diversity in the Southern Gulf of Mexico coral reefs” submitted in Zootaxa. This dataset contains information on 231 specimens of 80 species of the Demospongiae class, including their distribution in coral reefs in the Southern Gulf of Mexico, and their depth. All specimens are hosted in the National Collection of the Phylum Porifera Gerardo Green” (CNPGG), at the Instituto de Ciencias del Mar y Limnología, Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México, Mexico City." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Gulf of Mexico, Campeche Bank, Coral Reefs, Porifera" ;
    ecsummary:name "Porifera diversity and distribution data in the Southern Gulf of Mexico" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/5acccdb9-8230-4ec7-bea0-5bf3b0ce9d70> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:efaba55af6708e18ce8c8419549e26ccab130ad4>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This dataset is the  abundances of the range-shifting tropical rabbitfish Siganus fuscescens and compared these with the most important kelp consumers native of temperate reefs of Western Australia: Kyphosus sydneyanus and Olisthops cyanomelas. The study was carried out at temperate rocky reefs in southwestern Australia  where the rabbitfish S. fuscescens has established populations following a marine heatwave in 2011. See cited paper for methods and analysis." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Samplingevent, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Data from: Overwintering tropical herbivores accelerate detritus production on temperate reefs (2019)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/ebe4a98a-656a-45df-90b3-3f177375a405> ;
.

