<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:f62904759ed95d00d591d218c8194bd00b69a52b>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
Udayana University &amp; WWF Indonesia

Dataset credits:
Data provider
Udayana University - WWF Joint Program
Originating data center
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/">Satellite Tracking and Analysis Tool (STAT)</a>
Project partner
Udayana University has been involved in sea turtle conservation in Indonesia since early 1990s. Main arena are research and education/training.
Project sponsor or sponsor description
WWF Indonesia is the leading non-government organization in the country who committed to focus on sea turtle conservation in all aspects of turtle issues, i.e. habitat protection, trade reduction, and bycatch mitigation.


Abstract:
This project is part of the larger program entitled: TRACKING AND GENETIC ANALYSIS OF SEA TURTLES IN THE EASTERN PART OF INDONESIA, to identify post nesting migration of Olive, green and hawksbill turtles, as well as raising awareness of the locals to support turtle conservation in the region.

Supplemental information:
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/index.shtml?project_id=390">Visit STAT's project page</a> for additional information.

This dataset is a summarized representation of the telemetry locations aggregated per species per 1-degree cell.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Bali turtles (aggregated per 1-degree cell)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/519e0e77-1a8e-4d1f-b82d-0127655b8963> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:f62ded60f5128967c9e27dfef3d553af84d56255>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """This dataset was acquired on the RV Southern Surveyor voyage SS2012_T06. The aim was to characterize the bacterial community structure in surface waters along a 2500 km transect in the eastern Indian Ocean Full details of data, reports and publications of the voyage is at http://www.marine.csiro.au/data/trawler/survey_details.cfm?survey=SS2012_T06
Note on data download/processing:
Data downloaded from Australian Microbiome Initiative via Bioplatforms Australia Data Portal on 17 June 2022. The search filter applied to download data from Bioplatforms Australia Data portal are stored in the Darwin Core property (identificationRemarks). Taxonomy is assigned according to the taxonomic database (SILVA 138) and method (Sklearn) which is stored in the Darwin Core Extension
DNA derived data property (otu_db). Prefix were removed from the taxonomic names as shown in the example (e.g. d__Bacteria to Bacteria). Scientific name is assigned to the valid name available from the highest taxonomic rank.
This collection is published as Darwin Core Occurrence, so the event level measurements need to be replicated for every occurrence. Instead of data replication, the event level eMoF data are made available separately at https://www.marine.csiro.au/data/services/obisau/emof_export.cfm?ipt_resource=bioplatforms_mm_ss2012_t06""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "occurrence, 16S rRNA" ;
    ecsummary:name "Marine Microbes from RV Southern Surveyor voyage SS2012_T06, Australia (2012)" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/ab590832-cef4-4f05-b412-f956b3aa7e24> ;
.

