<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:f7ab2dd98726f976d6af3d5a07f2ae3db04047e8>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
Happywhale

Dataset credits:
Happywhale and contributors

Abstract:
Happywhale.com is a resource to help you know whales as individuals, and to benefit conservation science with rich data about individual whales.

Supplemental information:
Sightings and images were submitted to Happywhale by contributors. A portion of the Happywhale data were transferred to OBIS-SEAMAP upon the agreement between Happywhale and OBIS-SEAMAP.

There may be duplicate records among Happywhale datasets and other OBIS-SEAMAP datasets. The precision of date/time vary per record. Some records have date accuracy up to year only.

This dataset includes sightings and photos from the following 16 contributors in alphabetic order:

Catherine MacRae; Dirk-Jan Saaltink; Elizabeth Robinson; Emilia Mussoni; Espaço Talassa; Holly Morgan-Wynne; Kristy King; Lobosonda; Marilia Olio; Mitch Doucet; Pamela Le Noury; Roxane Rambert; Sabine+Ulf; Sarah Kather; Sea Fever Productions; Susan Parks""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence,PhotoID;Visual sighting, Observation, Occurrence" ;
    ecsummary:name "Happywhale - Sei whale in North Atlantic Ocean" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/b1c2c519-8276-4a89-99c4-24e18e6feb55> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:f7aee2c25314b675c82def4b97efc56945f5f007>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description "This data were collected on the sixth Nella Dan voyage of a long term field survey project being conducted by the Australian Antarctic Division, to collect distribution, abundance and population structure data for the krill Euphausia superba in the Prydz Bay region, Antarctica. A Rectangular Midwater Trawl (RMT 1+8) was used for the collection of … larval and post larval (juvenile and adult) krill Euphausia superba, and other zooplankton. Three haul methods were used. At each station a shallow downward oblique haul was taken from the surface to 200m. At selected stations a deep downward oblique haul from 200m to 1000m was taken to collect early developmental stages of Euphausia superba. When krill swarms were located at particular depths (by a Simrad EK 120 echosounder), specific aimed horizontal tows were made." ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Specimen" ;
    ecsummary:name "RMT Trawl catch from the 1986/87 V7 AAMBER voyage" ;
    ecsummary:place "No spatialCoverage" ;
    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/2f257fe1-dc7d-45a6-8218-5995e1574b32> ;
.

