    ecsummary:publisher "obis" ;
    ecsummary:subjectOf <https://obis.org/dataset/b695804a-2c12-4b7f-ba1b-4c2d2f6adb4c> ;
.

<urn:gleaner.io:oih:obis:data:f8b210164b533fdcaef44150a7d35e3a811c0414>
    a ecsummary:Dataset ;
    ecsummary:description """Original provider:
Dr Col Limpus

Dataset credits:
Data provider
GHD, Xstrata and  DERM nesting flatback monitoring
Originating data center
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/">Satellite Tracking and Analysis Tool (STAT)</a>
Project partner
The Matilda project is a partnership between TurtleCare Sunshine Coast, Sunshine Coast Regional Council and Queeensland's Department of Environment and Resource Management.


Abstract:
Matilda is a female Loggerhead turtle who was tagged and fitted with a tracker when she came up on Shelly Beach for what was probably her third nest of the season.

Supplemental information:
<a href="http://www.seaturtle.org/tracking/index.shtml?project_id=696">Visit STAT's project page</a> for additional information.

This dataset is a summarized representation of the telemetry locations aggregated per species per 1-degree cell.""" ;
    ecsummary:keywords "Occurrence, Observation" ;
    ecsummary:name "Sunshine Coast Council Turtle Tracking (aggregated per 1-degree cell)" ;
